  (:id "elixir/elixir-wire-fuzz-every-root" :type :task :title "Elixir rides the wire fuzzer over every root (v1.3)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "elixir-wire-fuzz-every-root" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-elixir" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-elixir" :tier "pro" :needs ("elixir-carries-maps-and-union-arms-on-the-table-wire-2" "elixir-carries-the-fixed-class-on-the-table-wire-2") :note "Moved from the sprint to the roadmap on 2026-10-17 by the owner's ruling (schema languages other than Go leave the sprint). Card elixir-wire-fuzz-every-root, column waiting at the move, stream schema-elixir, base sprint/schema-elixir, tier pro. Task: Bind the Elixir wire-fuzz arm to every root of the conformance harness's default roster (not the Card root alone), add tables-elixir-wire-fuzz-all to make/elixir.mk with the zero-coverage greps, make test-elixir run it, and flip the roadmap cell; a divergence is reported, never patched. Sprint order: after the held sentinel schema-elixir-go-first (Go first).")
  (:id "elixir/elixir-rides-the-wire-fuzzer-and-retains-on-every-root-2" :type :task :title "Elixir retains unknown fields on every root (v1.3): the retain core" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "elixir-rides-the-wire-fuzzer-and-retains-on-every-root-2" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-elixir" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-elixir" :tier "heavy" :needs ("elixir-carries-maps-and-union-arms-on-the-table-wire-2" "elixir-carries-the-fixed-class-on-the-table-wire-2" "elixir-wire-fuzz-every-root") :note "Moved from the sprint to the roadmap on 2026-10-17 by the owner's ruling (schema languages other than Go leave the sprint). Card elixir-rides-the-wire-fuzzer-and-retains-on-every-root-2, column waiting at the move, stream schema-elixir, base sprint/schema-elixir, tier heavy. Task: The retain core: make the retain and retain-save surfaces answer every retain row of the manifest on the Elixir driver, matching Go's retained and retain_lost counts on every construct family (repeated unions included), and add the --retain arm to tables-elixir-wire-fuzz-all. Sprint order: after the held sentinel schema-elixir-go-first (Go first).")
  (:id "elixir/elixir-retain-negative-control" :type :task :title "Elixir retain-unknown has a negative control (v1.3)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "elixir-retain-negative-control" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-elixir" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-elixir" :tier "pro" :needs ("elixir-rides-the-wire-fuzzer-and-retains-on-every-root-2") :note "Moved from the sprint to the roadmap on 2026-10-17 by the owner's ruling (schema languages other than Go leave the sprint). Card elixir-retain-negative-control, column waiting at the move, stream schema-elixir, base sprint/schema-elixir, tier pro. Task: Add tables-elixir-retain-negative-control to make/elixir.mk, built as ELIXIR_SABOTAGED_BUILD: sabotage the retaining save so it drops one retained field, run the --retain arm of tables-elixir-wire-fuzz-all and the retain surface, and pass only when retain goes red and no other surface does. Sprint order: after the held sentinel schema-elixir-go-first (Go first).")
  (:id "elixir/elixir-fixed-read-beats-its-packet-read" :type :task :title "Elixir: the fixed read is faster than its own packet read, identity and plan lanes judged separately" :state :doing :evidence nil :sprint-card "elixir-fixed-read-beats-its-packet-read" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-elixir" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-elixir" :tier "heavy" :needs ("elixir-read-arm-measures-identity-plan-and-packet-reads-alone") :pushed-head "8d0a2ea72b89a3a3092a9c6aaf88c89196a938f0" :note "Moved from the sprint to the roadmap on 2026-10-17 by the owner's ruling (schema languages other than Go leave the sprint). Card elixir-fixed-read-beats-its-packet-read, column waiting at the move, stream schema-elixir, base sprint/schema-elixir, tier heavy. Task: On a quiet Linux bench run the paired benchmark for the Elixir leg and record the board (identity, plan and packet read in ns/record) with the identity and plan lanes each judged faster than Elixir's own packet read, per BENCH-STANDARD.md, committing bench/results/packet-read-elixir/board.txt and the verdict. WORK EXISTS: last pushed head 8d0a2ea72b89a3a3092a9c6aaf88c89196a938f0; resume from it, do not start over. Sprint order: after the held sentinel schema-elixir-go-first (Go first).")
