  (:id "vt/c/generator-panic" :type :task :title "C: a red at the branch head that holds 31 cells" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/ctable/fixedroadmap_t18_test.go: TestFixedRoadmapCT18DirectArms (union-field-arms/c/valid-data, vt/c/generator-panic)" "make tables-c SERIALIZE_C=<serialize.c v1.10.0, the ci-full.yml pin> NODE=node (26.x, the js.mk override): exit 0, wire-fuzz 0 divergences; grep -rn table_fixed_put0 build/tables-generated-c/ prints nothing") :tested-revision "2d91bb71a7d0d665b06f3e56beab06aff1858094" :note "DONE: make tables-c ran green at 2d91bb71a with the serialize.c sibling staged at its pinned tag v1.10.0 (Rowan's hand run, 2026-10-14, darwin/arm64 clang). HISTORY, the red this leaf held: THE CODE RED IS FIXED, the red that remains is the absent serialize.c sibling. The R2.schema nil-arm panic and the direct-arm table_fixed_put0 gap are both fixed: internal/codegen/ctable/fixedform.go now carries an emitFixedWriteArm twin of the reference (internal/codegen/cpptable/fixedform.go:473) routing text, bytes and array arms through the arm's own unnamed struct, and the union case of emitFixedWriteElement calls it; TestFixedCT18DirectArmLines and TestFixedRoadmapCT18DirectArms/vt/c/generator-panic are green, and `grep -rn table_fixed_put0 build/tables-generated-c/` prints nothing after make build/tables-generated-c/.stamp. The next red is the ENVIRONMENT PREREQUISITE, not a code line: `make tables-c SERIALIZE_C=../serialize.c` stops at build/tables-generated-c/scalars/ScalarsTable.h:32: fatal error: serialize.h: No such file or directory (also scalars2/Scalars2Table.h:32, test/conformance/c/unit_scalars.c:2, test/conformance/c/unit_tblscalars2.c:1) because the serialize.c sibling checkout is absent in this worktree; every other conformance translation unit compiles clean under -Werror -Wshadow. The member must stage the serialize.c sibling and run `make tables-c SERIALIZE_C=<the staged sibling>`; when that run is green this leaf flips :done.")
  (:id "vt/c/strict-read" :type :task :title "C: the strict read surface (§6.5): the clamped-field slot (§2.13) and the named tolerant read (§16.11)" :state :todo :evidence nil :note "The C leg has no strict read: no read refuses a clamp by name (TableClampedField, `clamped: <Table>.<field>`) and no tolerant function is named apart from the plain one, so §2.13's clamped-field slot and §16.11's bound probes have no C surface to hold them. Found by the stage 2 lane c landing (PR #2144), 2026-10-21.")
  (:id "vt/c/report-reason" :type :task :title "C: the text form's refusal Reason strings (§16.3)" :state :todo :evidence nil :note "The C JSON read refuses ill-formed UTF-8 and a zero bound for text storage (carried-by=go,c since PR #2144), but its report has no Reason text: it answers Malformed alone, never `string_not_utf8: <key>`, `string_lone_surrogate: <key>` or `text_holds_zero: <Table>.<field>`.")
  (:id "vt/c/surrogates" :type :task :title "C: lone and out-of-order surrogate escapes refused by name (§16.3)" :state :todo :evidence nil :note "The C JSON read still turns a lone or out-of-order \\u surrogate escape into U+FFFD (table_json_scan_unit); §16.3 refuses it by name, string_lone_surrogate. The str-lone-*-surrogate hostile rows take carried-by= as ports land; C is not yet on them.")
