  (:id "vt/wire-fuzzer/elixir" :type :task :title "Elixir: the wire fuzzer gate" :state :todo :evidence nil :note "RED at the branch head over the default roster: make tables-elixir-wire-fuzz-all (the harness default roster, no --manifest; TestWireFuzzAllTargetElixir pins its wiring; 35 roster entries the leg cannot open pinned by name in test/conformance/elixir/wire-fuzz-absent.txt: 10 no-codec, 25 uncarried) fails on the first mutant, seed 24845619678: an empty wire (truncate #0) for tabledemo.WideBlob has the oracle load malformed with defaults while the leg's LoadMeasure refuses with measure -1. WireFuzz.codec/1 now reads the roster entry's form: form 1 binds <Package>.Table and form 2 binds <Package>.TableMessage (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §3.3), where the file codec used to be handed a form-2 wire it refuses as newer_form. The eight MANIFEST connection roots now open: the seven fixed message roots replay their pinned message with 0 divergences, while graphdemo.Scene's message reader answers :malformed for graph_tree_message (the Elixir message surface reports it absent at BASE too), so it diverges and is the FIFTH red cause beside the four codec causes; blobdemo.Catalog, a form-2 root that rides only in the pinned-vector index and whose unit declares no fixed table, has no TableMessage and is pinned absent by name. The message arm also has no per-kind counters and no message region measure, so it can diverge on those beside graphdemo.Scene; that is a codec surface gap for the green card, not a wiring one. The four codec causes the previous attempt recorded are unchanged: empty wire, LoadMeasure under-sizing, kind_mismatch not counted, malformed not set; each is its own fix card, never patched here. The Card root alone stays green under make cards-elixir-wire-fuzz. No negative control registered in make/negative-controls.json. Attempts w3 and w4 reconfirm the identical first-mutant divergence at seed 24845619678 (empty tabledemo.WideBlob wire, pass truncate #0). The four causes are carded: elixir-fix-empty-wire-loads-malformed-with-defaults, elixir-fix-load-measure-covers-the-framing-region, elixir-fix-unbounded-list-counts-kind-mismatch, elixir-fix-chain-p2-sets-malformed; this cell flips to done when make tables-elixir-wire-fuzz-all prints 0 divergences after they land AND the message-form gap (graphdemo.Scene's reader, the message arm's counters and region measure) is closed, so elixir-wire-fuzzer-all-roots-green cannot go green on the four cards alone.")
