  ; Moved from GitHub issues on 2026-10-15: one task per open issue that was real work not already on this page, grouped under the work-set "github-issues".
  (:id "issue/1139" :type :task :title "A go test -run pattern that matches no test fails its gate (#1139)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/1139" :note "The fix landed as #1847 (internal/ci/runpattern_test.go) and was dropped when the streams replaced main (8d76bacce); it is absent from main at 4d9941fbc, and nothing in internal/ci refuses a -run pattern that selects nothing. Recover it from archive/main-before-streams-2026-10-14 and re-pin it to today's Makefile. The js fixed-form targets already select TestJSFixedVersioning (make/js.mk:492).")
  (:id "issue/1008" :type :task :title "treelock: drop the two f.Sync() calls on the lock path (#1008)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/1008" :note "tools/treelock/main.go:128 and :152 still call f.Sync(), which is F_FULLFSYNC on darwin (p50 13.5 ms, worst 40 ms) and buys nothing: the pid line's one reader sees it through the page cache. Remove both, with a test that a second process observes the lock without a sync. Prior branch rowan/schema-1008-treelock-the-two-f-sync-calls-on-the@f4d12963 (PR #1039, closed unmerged).")
  (:id "issue/1004" :type :task :title "Enums take no | max headroom: the checker refuses it and every backend drops the headroom path (#1004)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/1004" :note "The spec half landed (#1005; docs/SPEC.md:1435 lists | max = K on an enum as refused), but the checker still accepts it: schema check on enum Color | max = 15 { Red, Green } exits 0 at 4d9941fbc. Owed: the refusal with its diagnostics row, the headroom read paths and their tests removed from every backend, and Count removed from enums and union tags (Glenn 2026-09-13: Just Max for enums).")
  (:id "issue/735" :type :task :title "American spelling sweep against today's tree (#735)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/735" :note "British spellings remain in prose and code (behaviour, licence and others in .github/workflows/ci-full.yml, Makefile, docs/SPEC-TABLES.md, docs/FAQ.md, bench/). One PR: prose, comments, goldens, tests, the Makefile and workflows, identifiers we own renamed under the compiler, goldens re-pinned, and the moved protocol ids named. Supersedes the stale #402.")
  (:id "issue/675" :type :task :title "examples: the Vec3 cpp_native mapping rides in the generated C++ (#675)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/675" :sprint-card "cpp-native-mapping-rides-in-the-generated-cpp" :sprint-stream "schema-c-cpp" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-cpp" :tier "heavy" :note "Back in the sprint 2026-10-16 as card cpp-native-mapping-rides-in-the-generated-cpp (stream schema-c-cpp; Glenn: bring the rest of the schema C++, C and Rust work into the sprint). examples/Types.schema:13 maps Vec3 to VecMath, but Vec3 is referenced only from its declaring file, so generated/cpp carries no VecMath and never includes vec_math.h. Move a Vec3 reference into another file of the unit, re-pin the nine languages' generated goldens, and add a control that the cpp_native header is included when a mapping is live. Same root as tutorial finding G-06 (#521).")
  (:id "issue/629" :type :task :title "Owner ruling: exact integer reading for integer fields in the text form (#629)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/629" :note "An integer field's JSON token is read through a double in the reference, C, Rust and Go (1e309 in a uint8 is kind_mismatch; 9007199254740993.0 in a 64-bit field rounds silently), while map keys already read exactly (#625). docs/SPEC-TABLES.md section 16.2 Numbers does not settle it. Owed: Glenn's ruling, then section 16.2 and all nine legs aligned, with a hostile-corpus row per case.")
  (:id "issue/610" :type :task :title "Owner ruling: one counted event or two when a 64-bit integer field's text value passes 64 bits (#610)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/610" :note "docs/SPEC-TABLES.md section 16.2 counts two events for the 128-bit kinds (the saturation, then the declared range) and is silent for int64 and uint64, where the reference counts two clamps today. The page says which, and the report pins follow. Suggested on the issue: one event per field.")
  (:id "issue/609" :type :task :title "Map keys wider than the text walker's 255-byte buffer: rule and gate (#609)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/609" :note "docs/SPEC-TABLES.md section 2.8 bounds a map key only by N, while both engines hold a key in 255 bytes, for string and integer keys alike. Options on the issue: drop with a named count, size the buffer by N, or refuse map[string(N at or above 255)] at compile time for the text form (suggested). Glenn's call, then sections 2.8 and 16.2 and the checker's refusal with its diagnostics row.")
  (:id "issue/594" :type :task :title "Resolve section 16.3 against section 3 on a U+0000 escape in a string(N) body (#594)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/594" :note "docs/SPEC-TABLES.md section 16.3 (near line 13909) writes and round-trips a narrow field's interior zero byte as the U+0000 escape, while section 3 (line 3741) makes a zero byte in a string payload damage, so a text can pack into a wire the reference refuses on read. Proposed on the issue: the wire rule wins and the text read refuses the escape by name. Needs Glenn's confirmation, then both readers, a json-hostile row and a negative control.")
  (:id "issue/558" :type :task :title "A hostile-bytes mutant fuzzer for the packet wire (#558)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/558" :note "Landed as 25c94863f (compiler/packettextfuzz_test.go, CARD-9057) and dropped when the streams replaced main (8d76bacce); absent from main at 4d9941fbc. Restore it from archive/main-before-streams-2026-10-14, with seeds pinned by name, the seed and mutant printed on a red, a run from make test and certification, and a negative control that plants a reader defect.")
  (:id "issue/547" :type :task :title "Generated code passes each language's standard formatter and analyzer, gated per leg (#547)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/547" :sprint-card "java-generated-code-is-format-and-lint-clean-and-the-gate-cannot-skip,elixir-generated-code-passes-credo-at-default-strictness,cs-generated-packet-units-pass-dotnet-format-and-the-analyzers" :sprint-stream "schema-java,schema-elixir,schema-cs" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java,sprint/schema-elixir,sprint/schema-cs" :tier "heavy" :note "Back in the sprint 2026-10-16 as cards java-generated-code-is-format-and-lint-clean-and-the-gate-cannot-skip (Java), elixir-generated-code-passes-credo-at-default-strictness (Elixir), cs-generated-packet-units-pass-dotnet-format-and-the-analyzers (C#) (streams schema-java, schema-elixir, schema-cs; Glenn: bring the rest of the schema Java, Elixir, C# work into the sprint). Glenn 2026-09-05: generated code reads as the language's own, red on any formatter or analyzer finding at default strictness (gofmt and vet, clippy, dart analyze and format, eslint, the .NET analyzers, the JDK lint, credo and mix format, clang-tidy for C and C++), with a dialect page per language. Go is the open sprint card generated-go-is-lint-clean-and-names-its-sources; Dart's fixed module is gates/dart-fixed-analyze; the other seven legs are owed here.")
  (:id "issue/546" :type :task :title "A diagnostic costs nothing on the read or write path, measured (#546)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/546" :note "Glenn 2026-09-05: if it costs speed on read or write, it is not worth it. Owed: the sentence in SPEC-TABLES.md's cost model and in PERFORMANCE.md, and a certification gate: a read and write regression check over the bench corpus for both wires, with a stated noise band and a planted-cost negative control.")
  (:id "issue/521" :type :task :title "Tutorial second-pass findings: re-verify G-03 to G-18 on main and fix what stands (#521)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/521" :note "Checked on main 4d9941fbc on 2026-10-15: G-01 (a flag after a path is now named), G-02 (one error), G-17 (no field-tagged TLV, internal/check/diagnostics_test.go:1015), G-19 (ruled as the contract, internal/tablewire/cycle_test.go, #535) and G-20 (Math.schema refused) are fixed; G-06 stands as #675. The rest are unverified; G-11, G-15 and G-16 overlap the variable-tables rows (the unit registry, the id-table wire, the refusal reasons).")
  (:id "issue/474" :type :task :title "One SPDX license expression everywhere, and a valid one in generated headers (#474)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/474" :note "The CAA half is done (docs/CONTRIBUTING.md:462). Still open: LICENSE grants AGPL-3.0-or-later while README.md:4 and :124 say AGPL-3.0 (Glenn picks one); generated headers carry SPDX-License-Identifier: NONE, which is not a valid SPDX expression (NOASSERTION is the idiom), to move with a release that re-pins the goldens; the compiler's own sources carry no SPDX header.")
  (:id "issue/472" :type :task :title "CAA workflow: least privilege for the org PAT (#472)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/472" :note "The SHA pins and the @latest ban are done and linted (go test ./internal/ci/, .github/workflows/ci-fast.yml:369-373). Owed, by Glenn's hand because the PAT is his: .github/workflows/cla.yml still runs on pull_request_target with actions: write and hands CLA_SIGNATURES_TOKEN to an archived third-party action (pinned at ca4a40a7). Scope the PAT down or replace the action with a first-party check, and drop actions: write.")
  (:id "issue/463" :type :task :title "Release gate: the corpus generated by the previous release and this one, byte-compared under an equal protocol id (#463)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/463" :note "The WireLaw line landed (docs/VERSIONING.md:142, internal/check/projection_test.go:189); docs/VERSIONING.md:146-151 and :1076 name this gate as owed. It runs in certify before the tag, with a negative control that changes one rounding rule without a shape change and goes red.")
  (:id "issue/449" :type :task :title "C++ and C: a generated per-arm union setter that sets the tag and the arm together (#449)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/449" :sprint-card "cpp-union-arm-setter-sets-tag-and-arm-together,c-union-arm-setter-mirrors-the-cpp-reference" :sprint-stream "schema-c-cpp" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-cpp,sprint/schema-c" :tier "heavy" :note "Back in the sprint 2026-10-16 as cards cpp-union-arm-setter-sets-tag-and-arm-together (C++, the reference) and c-union-arm-setter-mirrors-the-cpp-reference (C) (stream schema-c-cpp; Glenn: bring the rest of the schema C++, C and Rust work into the sprint). Generated C++ selects an arm by two assignments (generated/cpp/ArmDefaults.h:62 constructs the tag only), so a forgotten tag writes None and the payload is lost with no assert. Owed: a per-arm setter, a round-trip test that uses it, USAGE's union section showing it first, and C mirroring the reference (#447 F-08).")
  (:id "issue/431" :type :task :title "C++ reference consolidation review: spec against implementation, dead code, scaffolding (#431)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/431" :sprint-card "cpp-reference-consolidation-review" :sprint-stream "schema-c-cpp" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-cpp" :tier "heavy" :note "Back in the sprint 2026-10-16 as card cpp-reference-consolidation-review (stream schema-c-cpp; Glenn: bring the rest of the schema C++, C and Rust work into the sprint). Glenn 2026-09-04. Three independent readers (SPEC.md and SPEC-TABLES.md sentence by sentence against the C++ reference and the tool; dead code and scaffolding; API feel) and a fix round. It was sequenced before the port sweep; C, C# and Go now carry the variable class, so its findings apply to them too.")
  (:id "issue/420" :type :task :title "The allocation gate refuses to certify off the pinned runtime: C#, Java, Dart, Elixir (#420)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/420" :sprint-card "dart-allocation-gate-counts-scavenges-and-refuses-off-the-pinned-sdk,elixir-allocation-audit-refuses-off-the-pinned-otp,cs-allocation-gate-refuses-off-the-pinned-runtime" :sprint-stream "schema-dart,schema-elixir,schema-cs" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-dart,sprint/schema-elixir,sprint/schema-cs" :tier "heavy" :note "Back in the sprint 2026-10-16 as cards dart-allocation-gate-counts-scavenges-and-refuses-off-the-pinned-sdk (Dart), elixir-allocation-audit-refuses-off-the-pinned-otp (Elixir), cs-allocation-gate-refuses-off-the-pinned-runtime (C#) (streams schema-dart, schema-elixir, schema-cs; Glenn: bring the rest of the schema Dart, Elixir, C# work into the sprint). docs/PORTING.md:1335 holds cs, java, dart and elixir open on #420 (Go is done: tables-go-allocator). Each gate reads the runtime version and refuses to certify on any other, with an escape hatch that reports and does not certify. Prior branch rowan/schema-420-the-allocation-gate-refuses-to-certi@24557f89 (PR #1070, closed unmerged).")
  (:id "issue/419" :type :task :title "Text differential against a third implementation: every leg but JavaScript (#419)" :state :todo :evidence nil :origin "https://github.com/mas-bandwidth/schema/issues/419" :sprint-card "java-text-form-is-held-against-the-go-engine-on-random-instances,dart-text-differential-against-the-go-engine,elixir-text-differential-against-the-go-engine,cs-text-differential-against-the-go-engine" :sprint-stream "schema-java,schema-dart,schema-elixir,schema-cs" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java,sprint/schema-dart,sprint/schema-elixir,sprint/schema-cs" :tier "heavy" :note "Back in the sprint 2026-10-16 as cards java-text-form-is-held-against-the-go-engine-on-random-instances (Java), dart-text-differential-against-the-go-engine (Dart), elixir-text-differential-against-the-go-engine (Elixir), cs-text-differential-against-the-go-engine (C#) (streams schema-java, schema-dart, schema-elixir, schema-cs; Glenn: bring the rest of the schema Java, Dart, Elixir, C# work into the sprint). docs/PORTING.md:1307 holds cpp, c, rust, go, cs, java, dart and elixir open on #419 (js carries tables-js-json-differential). The same random-instance text differential per leg against the Go engine, with the tie-break negative control. Prior branch rowan/schema-419-text-differential-against-a-third-im@0bf7bb21 (PR #1073, closed unmerged).")
