  (:id "port/luau" :type :work-set :title "Full port of schema to Luau (the Roblox dialect of Lua)" :note "A full port of every surface, queued after Go is complete. Target: Luau, the Roblox dialect of Lua." :children ("port/luau/generator" "port/luau/runtime" "port/luau/conformance"))
  (:id "port/moo" :type :work-set :title "Full port of schema to moo (the deterministic Q48.16 fork of Luau)" :note "Not started. Glenn 2026-10-28: every port on main at parity before schema v3.0.0, moo among them (docs/PORT-MOO.md, THE LAYERS)." :children ("port/moo/generator" "port/moo/runtime" "port/moo/conformance"))
  (:id "port/lobster" :type :work-set :title "Full port of schema to Lobster" :note "Glenn 2026-10-19: add Lobster as a language. Every surface, at parity with the nine main ports (2026-10-28 parity brief); docs/PORT-LOBSTER.md is the design and docs/PORTING.md the lobster column." :children ("port/lobster/generator" "port/lobster/runtime" "port/lobster/conformance" "port/lobster/bench" "port/lobster/bench-cpp"))
  (:id "port/lobster/bench" :type :task :title "Lobster port: the packet and table bench legs (bench/lobster, bench/tables/lobster/leg) under the BENCH-STANDARD contract, JIT row" :state :doing :evidence nil :note "Landed on rowan/port-lobster-bench (2026-10-28): bench/lobster/run measures BenchMixed (family gen) and bench/tables/lobster/leg measures TableMixed on the tolerant wire (family table), both under the pin's default JIT with --runtime-no-asserts (linkage jit, checks contract), both golden-gated before the clock (make bench-lobster-gate on the ci-fast lobster row; bench-lobster-gate-negative-control in the lobster control group). Wired into bench/run.sh --only lobster, bench/tools/pass-driver.sh and bench/tables/run.sh by discovery; make shape-gate scans .lobster and refuses seconds_elapsed outside the runners. Owed: the first measured sitting, which is a fleet pass (no numbers are taken on the studio), and the --cpp row (port/lobster/bench-cpp). Not in bench/paired: the fixed-form paired leg is not built.")
  (:id "port/lobster/bench-cpp" :type :task :title "schema-lobster-bench-cpp: the --cpp ahead-of-time row of both Lobster bench legs" :state :todo :evidence nil :note "docs/PORT-LOBSTER.md THE HARNESS asks every timed Lobster row to run the default JIT AND the --cpp build. The pinned release v2026.8 cannot do the second alone: `lobster --cpp` writes <toolchain>/dev/compiled_lobster/src/compiled_lobster.cpp and the release archive carries no dev/ tree, and the output compiles only with the engine's full build (SDL, FreeType, OpenGL; cmake -DLOBSTER_TOCPP=ON) from an aardappel/lobster checkout at 0921f7dd5745. That is a heavy build and a fleet job: pin the checkout, build it on a bench machine, add the --cpp row (linkage cpp) beside the JIT row in bench/lobster/route.sh's two callers. Until then both legs print the card's name on stderr and no --cpp number.")
  (:id "port/lua/packet" :type :task :title "Lua 5.4 (vanilla) packet leg: the examples against the shared wire vectors" :state :todo :evidence nil :note "Built, not yet verified to the :done bar (2026-10-28, through schema#2237): packet types (internal/codegen/lua) read and write the shared wire goldens: internal/codegen/lua/read_test.go TestLuaTypeWireReadsTheGoldens, write_test.go TestLuaTypeWireWritesTheGoldens, each with its negative control; serialize.lua vendored at its pin (TestVendoredLuaSerializeIsThePin). Open: the packet finite-floats rule (the serialize sub-worker's). Target: vanilla Lua 5.4 (native 64-bit integers and bitwise operators; LuaJIT, which is Lua 5.1 based, is not covered by this column).")
