  (:id "port/lua/generator" :type :task :title "Lua 5.4 (vanilla) port: the generated code: schema generate emits this language for every surface (packet types, fixed tables, variable tables)" :state :todo :evidence nil :note "Built, not yet verified to the :done bar (2026-10-28, through schema#2237): schema generate --lang lua emits the packet modules, <Package>Tables.lua and the runtime for every unit of the tables conformance manifest (33 units, 0 refused; make build/conformance-lua); every generated unit stands alone (internal/codegen/luatable/standalone_test.go TestLuaUnitStandsAlone) and testgen writes passing tests (TestLuaTestgenWritesPassingTests). Open: the schema_leg_lua build tag and the generated tree (another sub-worker's). Target: vanilla Lua 5.4 (native 64-bit integers and bitwise operators; LuaJIT, which is Lua 5.1 based, is not covered by this column).")
  (:id "port/lua/runtime" :type :task :title "Lua 5.4 (vanilla) port: the runtime: bit reader and writer, the table wire, the text form and the block and cook forms" :state :todo :evidence nil :note "Built, not yet verified to the :done bar (2026-10-28, through schema#2237): internal/codegen/luatable/runtime/*.lua carries form 1 load/save, the fixed form, the message form, retain-unknown, the JSON and hand-editable text forms, block read/build and cook open/check/write; make test-lua runs internal/codegen/luatable and the wire-fuzz differential (tables-lua-wire-fuzz-differential). Open items are the port/lua/open/* entries. Target: vanilla Lua 5.4 (native 64-bit integers and bitwise operators; LuaJIT, which is Lua 5.1 based, is not covered by this column).")
  (:id "port/lua/conformance" :type :task :title "Lua 5.4 (vanilla) port: the conformance leg: the shared wire vectors the C++ reference writes, the packet-text, packet-wide and packet-defaults gates, the table goldens, and their negative controls" :state :todo :evidence nil :note "Built, not yet verified to the :done bar (2026-10-28, through schema#2237): test/conformance/lua/driver answers all eighteen surfaces (wire 98/98 +2 named blob_shared refusals, message 13/13, retain 8/8 and retain-save 2/2 with retain_message_tail absent by name, every other surface full); the shared hostile corpus runs in test-lua (schema-lua-runs-hostile-corpus). Open: port/lua/open/retain-message-cross-build, port/lua/open/message-form-plain-table, and the conformance negative control (another sub-worker's). Target: vanilla Lua 5.4 (native 64-bit integers and bitwise operators; LuaJIT, which is Lua 5.1 based, is not covered by this column).")
  (:id "port/lua" :type :work-set :title "Full port of schema to Lua 5.4 (vanilla)" :note "A full port of every surface; the Lua leg comes to main through schema#2237 (2026-10-28), and the port/lua/open/* entries are the work left at parity with the nine main ports. Target: vanilla Lua 5.4 (native 64-bit integers and bitwise operators; LuaJIT, which is Lua 5.1 based, is not covered by this column)." :children ("port/lua/generator" "port/lua/runtime" "port/lua/conformance" "port/lua/open/caller-owned-load" "port/lua/open/keyed-accessor" "port/lua/open/descriptor-constants" "port/lua/open/one-pointer-walk" "port/lua/open/arm-is-a-field-line" "port/lua/open/float32-bit-surgery" "port/lua/open/typed-save" "port/lua/open/accessor-agreement" "port/lua/open/forgery-fuzz" "port/lua/open/runtime-name-scan" "port/lua/open/zero-cost" "port/lua/open/usage" "port/lua/open/text-differential" "port/lua/open/runtime-home" "port/lua/open/release-tier" "port/lua/open/cards" "port/lua/open/bench-board" "port/lua/open/message-form-plain-table" "port/lua/open/retain-message-cross-build"))
  (:id "port/lua/open/caller-owned-load" :type :task :title "Lua: a caller-owned load, its allocation gate and a soak (PORTING.md M1, I1, I9, I14)" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luatable/alloc_test.go: TestLuaLoadAllocationFloor" "internal/codegen/luatable/alloc_test.go: TestLuaLoadAllocationNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/luatable/alloc_test.go: TestLuaLoadAllocationRefusesOffThePin" "internal/codegen/luatable/alloc_test.go: TestLuaLoadNarrowsTheReaderInPlace" "internal/codegen/luatable/soak_test.go: TestLuaLoadSoak" "internal/codegen/luatable/soak_test.go: TestLuaLoadSoakNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/luatable/reset_test.go: TestLuaResetEqualsTheConstructor") :note "Closed 2026-10-29 (PORTING.md M1, I1, I9, I14). load.lua narrows the one reader's limit instead of building views, and load.Load / load.LoadTolerant take a kept state (load.NewState) and the caller's value (put back to its defaults in place by D.reset): the by-value rows allocate exactly zero bytes a load and the rows that license a table per element, node or list a pinned ceiling; the soak is a pass count gated on the allocation count beside the live heap; the gate refuses to certify off the pinned 5.4.8. The wire differential reads every mutant into the previous mutant's leftovers and found a clamped wide bound aliased into the value.")
  (:id "port/lua/open/keyed-accessor" :type :task :title "Lua: keyed arrays index by key, refused at both ends (PORTING.md M5)" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luatable/keyed_test.go: TestLuaKeyedAccessorCoversBothEnds" "internal/codegen/luatable/keyed_test.go: TestLuaKeyedNegativeControls") :note "Closed 2026-10-29. D.keyed (runtime/descriptor.lua) and the module's Keyed(table, field): an unsigned compare of key-1 against E.Max refuses None and a key past Max at both ends in every build; each yields the key beside the element; three reversed plants turn exactly their own rows (PORTING.md M5).")
  (:id "port/lua/open/descriptor-constants" :type :task :title "Lua: the descriptors are held immutable (PORTING.md M13)" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luatable/constants_test.go: TestLuaDescriptorsAreConstants" "internal/codegen/luatable/constants_test.go: TestLuaDescriptorsAreSealed" "internal/codegen/luatable/constants_test.go: TestLuaDescriptorsConstantNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/luatable/constants_test.go: TestLuaRuntimeBuildsNoDescriptorOnFirstUse") :note "Closed 2026-10-29. The generated module ends with D.seal (runtime/descriptor.lua): derived facts built once, every data table frozen against new keys by a __newindex that refuses; the overwrite half is the fingerprint gate over every runtime surface. The CRC table and the fixed layout tree, the two lazy builds the audit found, are built at require (PORTING.md M13).")
  (:id "port/lua/open/one-pointer-walk" :type :task :title "Lua: one walk for the numbering, the cook sizing and the cook pack (PORTING.md M15)" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luatable/onewalk_test.go: TestLuaOnePointerWalk" "internal/codegen/luatable/onewalk_test.go: TestLuaOnePointerWalkRowsAgreeWithTheEngine" "internal/codegen/luatable/onewalk_test.go: TestLuaOnePointerWalkNegativeControl") :note "Closed 2026-10-29. The numbering, the retaining save, the cook layout and pack and the JSON reference count are one walk, internal/codegen/luatable/runtime/descriptor.lua D.number_nodes (PORTING.md M15); the audit found save.lua and cookwrite.lua, and the same copy was in retain.lua and json.lua. The grouped-walk plant turns stream_arm_first red on the saved wire and the cook.")
  (:id "port/lua/open/arm-is-a-field-line" :type :task :title "Lua: a union arm is read through the field reader (PORTING.md M18)" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luatable/armfield_test.go: TestLuaArmIsAFieldLine" "internal/codegen/luatable/armfield_test.go: TestLuaArmFramingAgreesWithTheEngine" "internal/codegen/luatable/armfield_test.go: TestLuaArmFramingNegativeControl") :note "Closed 2026-10-29. load.lua read_payload is the one reader of a field's payload; read_field and read_arm both call it, the arm with its L standing in for the field's length (PORTING.md M18). The scan holds neither names a per-shape reader; the framing plants turn exactly their own rows against the engine. Found on the way, open: a union arm named `tag` shares the discriminator's key (roadmap port/lua/open/arm-named-tag).")
  (:id "port/lua/open/float32-bit-surgery" :type :task :title "Lua: float32 table cells move by bit surgery (PORTING.md M21)" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luatable/float32conv_test.go: TestLuaFloat32ConversionIsExactForEveryFinitePattern" "internal/codegen/luatable/floatspecial_test.go: TestLuaPlainFloatSpecialValuesAgreeAcrossForms" "internal/codegen/luatable/floatspecial_test.go: TestLuaFiniteFloatNegativeControl") :note "Settled 2026-10-29 with the finite-only rule: M21 retires on the table wire. A NaN or an infinity is refused on its raw bits before string.unpack('<f') converts it, in every read, and every writer refuses one, so the conversion only ever sees a finite float32, which it moves exactly (the sweep test). The packet runtime's bit surgery is the type wire's own and is unchanged. docs/PORTING.md M21 lua cell is the retired cell.")
  (:id "port/lua/open/typed-save" :type :task :title "Lua: a typed table save fast path (PORTING.md M22)" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luatable/typedsave_test.go: TestLuaTypedSaveEqualsDescriptorSave" "internal/codegen/luatable/typedsave_test.go: TestLuaTypedSaveNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/luatable/typedsave_test.go: TestLuaTypedSaveRunsFewerInstructions") :note "Closed 2026-10-29. internal/codegen/luatable/typedsave.go emits TypedBodies and SaveTyped<Name> into every unit's module (PORTING.md M22): scalar leaves written straight from the value with constants, every other field through the descriptor walk; save.SaveTyped runs them and save.Save stays descriptor-driven. Equal bytes and refusals over every manifest instance, defaults and moved leaves; three reversed plants; 64% of the walk's VM instructions. The id table is a map (a scan of the list was quadratic in the fields) and a one-byte LEB128 or a byte is a table read, in both paths.")
  (:id "port/lua/open/accessor-agreement" :type :task :title "Lua: generated block and cook accessors held against the descriptors (PORTING.md M11, J1)" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luatable/layoutagree_test.go" "make/lua-open-gates.mk:tables-lua-accessor-descriptor-agreement") :note "Closed 2026-10-29 in the Lua form: Lua generates no accessor (the block and cook are read through the descriptors alone), so the gate holds the layout's two independent derivations together, the compiler's (ir.Blocks, ir.RecordLayout) against the Lua runtime's own arithmetic, for every block projection, block row and cook record of the corpus. tables-lua-accessor-negative-control moves RenderCamera.camera_id four bytes and tables-lua-slot-negative-control moves TreeNode.left's descriptor offset eight; each reds on that field alone. The first run found B.Layout sizing a 128-bit integer, a 128-bit fixed and a bits(N) slot wrong; fixed in runtime/block.lua.")
  (:id "port/lua/open/forgery-fuzz" :type :task :title "Lua: the block and cook forgery fuzz oracle (PORTING.md I3)" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luatable/forgeryfuzz_test.go" "make/lua-open-gates.mk:tables-lua-fuzz") :note "Closed 2026-10-29. internal/codegen/luatable/forgeryfuzz_test.go fuzzes 2 block images and 4 cooks (24,000 mutants at seed 0x4c5541464f524745): a block must refuse or open whole against ir.Blocks, a cook must agree with the tool's cook-check, and a full walk of what opened reads inside the bytes. tables-lua-fuzz-negative-control removes both halves of the block's extent bound and, separately, the cook Check's region scan. The first run found Check opening a cook whose alignment word was forged (data part not a whole number of the alignment); fixed in runtime/cook.lua.")
  (:id "port/lua/open/runtime-name-scan" :type :task :title "Lua: claimed runtime names scanned both ways with a control (PORTING.md I6)" :state :done :evidence ("compiler/tablesluanames_test.go" "internal/tablenames/lua.go" "make/lua-open-gates.mk:tables-lua-names") :note "Closed 2026-10-29. compiler/tablesluanames_test.go reads every module-table key the Lua table emitter spells out of the emitted text (the unit module, its view and each runtime file, over the whole corpus) and holds it to tablenames.LuaModuleKeys both ways; every Lua spelling is a key of a returned module table, so none claims a name, and the one claimable spelling, a runtime module's file name, is refused beside a table and kept in a table-free unit. TestLuaRuntimeNameScanGoesRed plants an unregistered key in each convention and a registered name nothing emits.")
  (:id "port/lua/open/zero-cost" :type :task :title "Lua: the zero-cost gate (PORTING.md I10)" :state :done :evidence ("compiler/tableslua_test.go" "make/lua-open-gates.mk:tables-lua-zero-cost") :note "Closed 2026-10-29. TestLuaTablesMoveNoGeneratedPacketByte: adding a table moves no byte of the non-table output and grows only the table module and the embedded runtime, a table-free unit emits none of them, and the table module spells no block or cook symbol. TestLuaZeroCostGateGoesRed plants a moved packet byte, a vanished packet file and a stray non-table file.")
  (:id "port/lua/open/usage" :type :task :title "Lua: the documented surface compiles and runs (PORTING.md I12)" :state :done :evidence ("make/lua.mk tables-lua-usage" "make/lua.mk tables-lua-usage-negative-control" "docs/USAGE.md lua-table-usage") :roadmap-cell "none" :note "docs/USAGE.md carries a Lua section and a marked cook example (lua-table-usage); make tables-lua-usage extracts the fragment, wraps it in a script that reads a cookgen Scene cook (cook-checked by schema cook-check first) and supplies the one helper the page leaves to the caller, and runs it under the pinned Lua 5.4.8 against the generated tables/pointers modules it requires. tables-lua-usage-negative-control points the gate at two edited copies of the page (a renamed uncook.Read, and a walk of a field the Scene does not have) and requires each to fail. test-lua runs the gate; tables-lua-release runs both.")
  (:id "port/lua/open/text-differential" :type :task :title "Lua: a random text differential against the Go engine (PORTING.md I13)" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luatable/textdifferential_test.go" "make/lua-open-gates.mk:tables-lua-json-differential") :note "Closed 2026-10-29. TestLuaTextDifferential draws 200 random float instances in Lua (the Elixir leg's splitmix64 seed) and byte-compares the engine's text with the leg's and the engine's pack of the leg's text with the leg's wire; 5,000 more at a second seed were clean. TestLuaTextDifferentialNegativeControl caps a float32 at six digits and goes red on 199 of 200.")
  (:id "port/lua/open/runtime-home" :type :task :title "Lua: the runtime home with a file-order control (PORTING.md J2)" :state :done :evidence ("make/lua-open-gates.mk:tables-lua-runtime-home" "make/lua-open-gates.mk:tables-lua-runtime-home-negative-control") :note "Closed 2026-10-29. The table module stays <Package>Tables.lua and every embedded runtime file stays byte-identical when an earlier-sorting schema file joins the unit; the control puts the file-order rule back through go build -overlay and the module moves from GuardedTables.lua to AaaTables.lua.")
  (:id "port/lua/open/release-tier" :type :task :title "Lua: a bench leg and the tables-lua-release tier (PORTING.md I8, J3)" :state :done :evidence ("make/lua.mk tables-lua-release" "make/lua.mk tables-lua-bench-gate" "make/lua.mk tables-lua-bench-gate-negative-control" "bench/tables/lua/table_main.lua" ".github/workflows/certify.yml release-gates") :roadmap-cell "none" :note "bench/tables/lua is the tables bench leg (leg build/run, table_main.lua: the tolerant wire of bench/corpus/BenchTable.schema, 1 warmup + 7 runs, CSV v2 rows write and round_trip, corpus_id equal to the C leg's). tables-lua-bench-gate (the correctness gate, no clock) rides test-lua with a two-witness control; tables-lua-release scales the PR tier (the wire-fuzz differential at ten times the count and a second seed, the usage gate and its witnesses, the bench gate and its witnesses) and takes the measured pass (bench/tables/run.sh --only lua --bare). certify.yml derives the target from the Makefile and installs the Lua pin for it. bench/tools/shapegate now scans .lua and os.clock. The labelled board file (I8) is port/lua/open/bench-board.")
  (:id "port/lua/open/cards" :type :task :title "Lua: the card facade and its cards driver (PORTING.md J6)" :state :done :evidence ("make/lua.mk cards-lua-conformance" "make/lua.mk cards-lua-conformance-negative-control" "make/lua.mk cards-lua-conformance-upgrade-negative-control" "make/lua.mk cards-lua-conformance-hash-negative-control" "tables/cards/lua/cards_test.lua") :roadmap-cell "none" :note "tables/cards/lua: cards.lua (the owning facade: Load, FromJSON, ToJSON, Wire, Parse, Render, Upgrade, ReadStrict, TaskHash with a pure-Lua SHA-256, the six Set* edits), driver and driver.lua (nine surfaces, the generated view read from the descriptors), cards_test.lua (eight unit tests, no clock or process). The harness cards subcommand passes all 43 cases on all nine surfaces; make cards-conformance-all runs the Lua leg. Running it found two retain.lua faults, both fixed in internal/codegen/luatable/runtime/retain.lua: wire_nodes did not skip the node table's leading count (it read the count as a node), and capture counted the unit's own string and bytes blob nodes as retain_lost.")
  (:id "port/lua/open/bench-board" :type :task :title "Lua: the labelled bench board (PORTING.md I8)" :state :todo :evidence nil :note "Open 2026-10-29. The leg is registered and gated (port/lua/open/release-tier) but no measured sitting has been taken: the board file bench/tables/results/<date>-pairing-lua-<arch>-<host>.md, labelled PAIRING CHECK, not a sitting, in its first line and it certifies nothing in its third, is written from the rows tables-lua-release prints in a certify run. Benches do not run on the studio.")
    (:id "port/lua/open/arm-named-tag" :type :task :title "Lua: a union arm named tag keeps the discriminator (SPEC-TABLES §2.6)" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luatable/armslot_test.go: TestLuaArmSlotKeepsTheDiscriminator") :note "Closed 2026-10-29. A Lua union value is { tag = <arm index>, <slot> = <payload> } and each arm descriptor now carries its slot: the arm's name, except an arm named tag, whose slot is the name with underscores appended until it names no arm (luatable.armSlots). Every reader and writer that stores or reads the payload goes through arm.slot; the wire, the text and the JSON still name the arm. Reversed witness: without the slot the stream_arm_tag row refuses on wire, json-read, json-write and cook-write. The shared conformance row stream_arm_tag is proposed to main in #2358; whether another port collides is that port's conformance leg.")
  (:id "port/lua/open/message-form-plain-table" :type :task :title "Lua: a message-form request naming a plain table is refused by name (SPEC-TABLES §3.3, §11)" :state :todo :evidence nil :note "Open 2026-10-28 (Lua parity audit). runtime/message.lua loadMessages, measureMessages and saveMessages do not check T.MessageRoots, so the message form reads a plain table (graph_tree on Scene answers bytes where the Go reference answers absent, plain table). The refusal needs a reason name the spec does not yet give; C, C++ and C# share the gap.")
  (:id "port/lua/open/retain-message-cross-build" :type :task :title "Lua: the announcement read resolves the sender's announced entries (SPEC-TABLES §3.3)" :state :todo :evidence nil :note "Open 2026-10-28 (Lua parity audit). AnnounceRead counts the announced entries but installs the receiver's own vocabulary (runtime/message.lua:1029), so a batch from another build is not read against its announcement; retain_message_tail answers absent by name. Its root is a plain table, so the Go reference answers that row absent too.")
