  (:id "sprint-out/c-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :type :task :title "sprint/schema-c takes sprint/schema-go: the C base forward-merge" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "c-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-c-cpp" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-c" :tier "heavy" :needs "none" :pushed-head "a29a922da20c1fcfc2270cd2105f7cff0f2419f6" :pushed-branch "sprint/c-base-forward-merge-schema-go.w7.g2.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/c-base-forward-merge-schema-go.w7.g2.e21 head a29a922da20c1fcfc2270cd2105f7cff0f2419f6 (attempt 10, review). Task: sprint/schema-c takes sprint/schema-go: the C base forward-merge. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card c-base-forward-merge-schema-go of stream schema-c-cpp was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE TASK. sprint/schema-c is about 686 commits behind sprint/schema-go (64dc1ddd when carded; GO TIP below is the tip you fetch, at or after it). Merge origin/sprint/schema-go into the base as ONE merge commit on the card branch: git fetch origin, then git merge --no-ff GO TIP. Never a rebase, never a squash, never a force-push. A trial merge on 2026-10-18 left these conflicts (a newer GO TIP may add a few; resolve those by the same rules): ROADMAP.md, internal/codegen/ctable/fixedform.go. Resolve each conflict keeping BOTH sides' intent, by these rules and no others: shared Go and IR code (ir/, internal/check/, internal/parser/, compiler/, internal/codegen/gotable/, tools/, .github/) takes GO TIP's version; port-specific code keeps the port's version, adapted to the new IR; spec text (docs/*.md) merges both rewrites, each statement true of the merged code; ROADMAP.md is regenerated with make roadmap, never hand-edited; the roadmap sexp ledgers (docs/roadmap.sexp, docs/roadmap-evidence/*.sexp) keep each row's true state at the merge head. internal/codegen/ctable/fixedform.go: the C base threads a `depth` argument into fixedLoopVar, GO TIP carries a g.fixedLoop counter and emitFixed [...]" :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
