  (:id "sprint-out/elixir-blob-named-twice-is-blob-shared" :type :task :title "Elixir: one blob named from two slots is blob_shared" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "elixir-blob-named-twice-is-blob-shared" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-elixir" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-elixir" :tier "pro" :needs "elixir-base-forward-merge-schema-go,elixir-plain-load-is-the-strict-read" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card elixir-blob-named-twice-is-blob-shared of stream schema-elixir, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "SOURCE (Glenn, 2026-10-18: \"We do all features across all languages\"). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md at d808c3f54 (schema-go), which arrives on this base with elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f; schema-go's behaviour there is the oracle. Never write spec text: a section that is silent or stale is reported, not edited. Family other rules, blob_shared: docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.5 (A blob is OWNED BY ONE SLOT: every writer refuses to emit it; the tolerant read keeps the one node and counts each extra naming in the report's blob_shared counter; the strict read refuses it) and §16.7; oracle internal/codegen/gotable/blobnamedtwice_test.go (TestBlobNamedTwiceSeed24, TestBlobNamedTwiceWriters)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
