  (:id "sprint-out/elixir-timestamp-text-is-strict-rfc3339" :type :task :title "Elixir: timestamp text is strict RFC 3339 section 5.6 date-time, and the elixir target carries timestamp" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "elixir-timestamp-text-is-strict-rfc3339" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-elixir" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-elixir" :tier "pro" :needs "elixir-base-forward-merge-schema-go,schema-go-target-names-what-it-carries,elixir-carries-timestamp-on-the-wire,elixir-plain-load-is-the-strict-read" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card elixir-timestamp-text-is-strict-rfc3339 of stream schema-elixir, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "SOURCE (Glenn, 2026-10-18: \"We do all features across all languages\"). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md at d808c3f54 (schema-go), which arrives on this base with elixir-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f; schema-go's behaviour there is the oracle. Never write spec text: a section that is silent or stale is reported, not edited. Family rfc3339, second half: docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.11 and §16.2 (7fb89e941): the JSON text of a timestamp is strict RFC 3339 §5.6 date-time, and a text that is not is refused by name, timestamp_not_rfc3339. Oracles internal/rfc3339 TestStrictRFC3339 (its case table), TestGoTimestampStrictRFC3339 and TestTextFormTimestampStrictRFC3339." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/java-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :type :task :title "sprint/schema-java takes sprint/schema-go: the Java base forward-merge" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "java-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-java" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java" :tier "heavy" :needs "none" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card java-base-forward-merge-schema-go of stream schema-java, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE TASK. sprint/schema-java is about 686 commits behind sprint/schema-go (64dc1ddd when carded; GO TIP below is the tip you fetch, at or after it). Merge origin/sprint/schema-go into the base as ONE merge commit on the card branch: git fetch origin, then git merge --no-ff GO TIP. Never a rebase, never a squash, never a force-push. A trial merge on 2026-10-18 left these conflicts (a newer GO TIP may add a few; resolve those by the same rules): ROADMAP.md, docs/PORTING.md, docs/roadmap.sexp. Resolve each conflict keeping BOTH sides' intent, by these rules and no others: shared Go and IR code (ir/, internal/check/, internal/parser/, compiler/, internal/codegen/gotable/, tools/, .github/) takes GO TIP's version; port-specific code keeps the port's version, adapted to the new IR; spec text (docs/*.md) merges both rewrites, each statement true of the merged code; ROADMAP.md is regenerated with make roadmap, never hand-edited; the roadmap sexp ledgers (docs/roadmap.sexp, docs/roadmap-evidence/*.sexp) keep each row's true state at the merge head. docs/PORTING.md: merge both rewrites; the Java section keeps the base's statement of what Java carries, the shared text takes GO TIP's. Then reg [...]" :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/java-blob-named-twice-is-refused" :type :task :title "One blob record named from two slots: Java's writers refuse it, the tolerant read counts it, the strict read refuses blob_shared" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "java-blob-named-twice-is-refused" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-java" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java" :tier "pro" :needs "java-base-forward-merge-schema-go,java-plain-variable-read-is-strict" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card java-blob-named-twice-is-refused of stream schema-java, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "SOURCE (Glenn, 2026-10-18): \"We do all features across all languages.\" Full parity of the Java port with schema-go at d808c3f54 (the oracle, which reaches this base through java-base-takes-schema-go-d808c3f). The standard is docs/SPEC-TABLES.md and docs/USAGE.md at that commit." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "java/per-value-shared-marker" :type :task :title "java: per-value shared marker so caller-built equal strings save by value" :state :todo :evidence nil :note "Rowan ruling 2026-10-21 (stage 2, PR #2154): the Java writers number a *string or *bytes slot by the identity of the String or byte[] it holds, so two slots holding one object are blob_shared (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.5, docs/USAGE.md Java). The wart: Java interns literals, so one literal set into two *string slots is one String and is refused. This row gives the tolerant load a per-value marker for a blob the WIRE shared, so a later save still refuses that (as the oracle does) while caller-built equal strings save by value as two records. Today: internal/codegen/javatable/blobshared_test.go TestJavaWritersRefuseASharedBlob pins the identity refusal, literal included. Rendered as the Java cell of the variable-tables row string-identity; the other languages' cells of that row take their blobs task, since the wart is Java's interning.")
