  (:id "sprint-out/schema-c-cpp-cs-base64-tolerant-read-follows-spec-16-2" :type :task :title "The C, C++ and C# tolerant text read does not follow section 16.2: the test/table-base64 harness fails 165 of 990 cases on each" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-c-cpp-cs-base64-tolerant-read-follows-spec-16-2" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-shared" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-shared" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-shared-base64-harness-follows-spec-16-2" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-c-cpp-cs-base64-tolerant-read-follows-spec-16-2 of stream schema-shared, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "Source. The coordinator, 2026-10-19, from the receipts of schema-shared-base64-harness-follows-spec-16-2 (r1). On each of C, C++ and C# the harness fails 165 of 990 cases:
- `invalid-padding-Q=Q==`, `invalid-padding-Q=Q=A=A=` and `invalid-padding-QQ==Q`: should be base64_not_canonical, accepted by the tolerant read and counted. The ports count a kind_mismatch instead (want 0), the decoded payload differs and the writer differs from the canonical Base64.
- `invalid-20` fails too (read the harness case and the receipts for what it expects).
- 161 cases must be malformed (control bytes `invalid-00..1f`, non-UTF-8 `invalid-80..ff`, the bare backslash `invalid-5c`), and these ports report malformed=0." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-c-generated-cbmc-readers-t" :type :task :title "C CBMC on the generated readers (c port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-c-generated-cbmc-readers-t" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-c-cpp" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-c" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "72d2a3ec4b38c0d6764da78ec753698cdfdc4063" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-c-generated-cbmc-readers-t.w5.g3.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-c-generated-cbmc-readers-t.w5.g3.e21 head 72d2a3ec4b38c0d6764da78ec753698cdfdc4063 (attempt 8, review). Task: C CBMC on the generated readers (c port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-c-generated-cbmc-readers-t of stream schema-c-cpp was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: CBMC bounded model checking of the generated C readers (memory safety, overflow, assertion checks with unwinding bounds stated per reader) over the generated c output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one). CBMC is heavy: nightly only." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-c-generated-clang-analyzer-and-eva" :type :task :title "C clang analyzer, gcc -fanalyzer and Frama-C EVA (c port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-c-generated-clang-analyzer-and-eva" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-c-cpp" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-c" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "b4365557e26796fbf4ca5eb757439831c463e564" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-c-generated-clang-analyzer-and-eva.w1.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-c-generated-clang-analyzer-and-eva.w1.g1.e21 head b4365557e26796fbf4ca5eb757439831c463e564 (attempt 1, review). Task: C clang analyzer, gcc -fanalyzer and Frama-C EVA (c port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-c-generated-clang-analyzer-and-eva of stream schema-c-cpp was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: the clang static analyzer (scan-build or --analyze), gcc -fanalyzer and Frama-C EVA (the proof that no runtime error is reachable in the generated readers) over the generated c output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one). Frama-C 33 is already installed on hetzner2 and amd-2; install it on the rest of the fleet. EVA is heavy: it runs nightly, the analyzers run per push if they fit the budget." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-c-generated-weverything-cppcheck-gate" :type :task :title "C Weverything and cppcheck gate (c port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-c-generated-weverything-cppcheck-gate" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-c-cpp" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-c" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "1c53af4c7f9ee037aaf07adb840c9efea8f0b4c6" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-c-generated-weverything-cppcheck-gate.w1.g3.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-c-generated-weverything-cppcheck-gate.w1.g3.e21 head 1c53af4c7f9ee037aaf07adb840c9efea8f0b4c6 (attempt 1, review). Task: C Weverything and cppcheck gate (c port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-c-generated-weverything-cppcheck-gate of stream schema-c-cpp was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: clang -Weverything -Werror (with a reviewed, justified list of -Wno- exceptions) and cppcheck over the generated c output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-c-ludicrous-int128-sign-extension-pinned" :type :task :title "C ludicrous test pins the int128 sign extension of a negative int64" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-c-ludicrous-int128-sign-extension-pinned" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-c-cpp" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-c" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "d4fb8f7c478216feda3bc689d6aea5cde1b77017" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-c-ludicrous-int128-sign-extension-pinned.w1.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-c-ludicrous-int128-sign-extension-pinned.w1.g1.e21 head d4fb8f7c478216feda3bc689d6aea5cde1b77017 (attempt 1, review). Task: C ludicrous test pins the int128 sign extension of a negative int64. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-c-ludicrous-int128-sign-extension-pinned of stream schema-c-cpp was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "TEST-ONLY. No emitter, runtime or generated file is edited." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-c-nightly-fuzz" :type :task :title "nightly fuzzing (c port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-c-nightly-fuzz" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-c-cpp" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-c" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "8a065d1b42f44038a5219d1689a09ae1c70bd718" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-c-nightly-fuzz of stream schema-c-cpp, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. It carried an earlier head: schema-c-nightly-fuzz attempt 3 head 8a065d1b42f44038a5219d1689a09ae1c70bd718. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "NIGHTLY FUZZING (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Fuzz the c port's generated readers with its native coverage-guided fuzzer: libFuzzer with ASan and UBSan (clang), plus AFL++. Targets: load, strict read and text/JSON parse for every table in a fuzz corpus schema set (pick the set from the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus) so that every table shape is covered, and list it in a file the harness reads). Seed the fuzzer from the Go fuzz corpus (internal/fuzz/testdata and the go test -fuzz seeds) and the conformance vectors. Both fuzzers drive the same harness functions; AFL++ is an additional nightly run." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-c-resource-bounds" :type :task :title "c port: bounded memory and time on hostile inputs (c port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-c-resource-bounds" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-c-cpp" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-c" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-c-resource-bounds of stream schema-c-cpp, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "Denial-of-service hardening for the c port (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Using the bounds documented by schema-shared-resource-bounds-every-port (read it first), assert in this port that hostile inputs cost bounded memory and time: huge counts, deep nesting, recursion, giant strings and many unknown fields. Allocation is bounded by input size times the documented factor; nesting depth is capped and refused by name. Use a test with an allocation counter in this language (an allocator hook, a counting allocator, runtime memstats, GC counters or the nearest the language offers; name it). Time is asserted by operation count or step count, never by wall clock. A violation is a finding: red first, then fix in the generator or runtime; fix the port, and carry any cross-port gap as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <one line>." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-c-runs-hostile-corpus" :type :task :title "c port runs the whole hostile corpus in its unit tier (c port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-c-runs-hostile-corpus" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-c-cpp" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-c" :tier "pro" :needs "c-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :pushed-head "defb7fbbce98e89f55acb0f3ff5cc75d203ec95f" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-c-runs-hostile-corpus of stream schema-c-cpp, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. It carried an earlier head: schema-c-runs-hostile-corpus attempt 3 head defb7fbbce98e89f55acb0f3ff5cc75d203ec95f. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "Make the c port run every input of the committed hostile corpus (built by schema-shared-hostile-corpus; read docs/HOSTILE-CORPUS.md and the manifest first) in its unit tier: for each input, the port's generated reader must reach the verdict the manifest holds (accept with the same decoded value digest, or refuse with the same named reason). The runner reads files only (no network, no real time). A mismatch is a finding: red first where it is a reader bug, carried as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <input> <one line>. Do not edit the corpus here; a wrong manifest verdict is reported against the engine card." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-c-tables-generate-c-macro-defined" :type :task :title "make tables-block-zero-cost runs the C emitter in its block-less arm" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-c-tables-generate-c-macro-defined" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-c-cpp" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-c" :tier "pro" :needs "c-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-c-tables-generate-c-macro-defined of stream schema-c-cpp, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "OWNER RULE (Glenn 2026-10-18): \"We do all features across all languages.\" and (2026-10-15) golang is first; this card changes no emitter, runtime or spec, only the Makefile wiring that lets the C arm of an existing gate run." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-cpp-conformance-sanitizers-asan-ubsan-msan" :type :task :title "C++ sanitizers over the conformance tests (cpp port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-cpp-conformance-sanitizers-asan-ubsan-msan" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-c-cpp" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-cpp" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "546211afb631f2a66bd9dc3df0c51ae76f06d3b9" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-cpp-conformance-sanitizers-asan-ubsan-msan.w7.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-cpp-conformance-sanitizers-asan-ubsan-msan.w7.g1.e21 head 546211afb631f2a66bd9dc3df0c51ae76f06d3b9 (attempt 7, review). Task: C++ sanitizers over the conformance tests (cpp port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-cpp-conformance-sanitizers-asan-ubsan-msan of stream schema-c-cpp was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: AddressSanitizer, UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer and MemorySanitizer builds of the generated C++ run through the conformance tests over the generated cpp output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one). MSan needs an instrumented libc++; build it once and cache it. MSan runs nightly; ASan+UBSan per push if they fit the budget." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-cpp-generated-clang-tidy-weverything-gate" :type :task :title "C++ clang-tidy and Weverything gate (cpp port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-cpp-generated-clang-tidy-weverything-gate" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-c-cpp" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-cpp" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "100b881423f5a15d6539002b10adfbee6799ded8" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-cpp-generated-clang-tidy-weverything-gate of stream schema-c-cpp, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. It carried an earlier head: schema-cpp-generated-clang-tidy-weverything-gate attempt 4 head 100b881423f5a15d6539002b10adfbee6799ded8. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: clang-tidy with the bugprone, cert and cppcoreguidelines check families, and clang -Weverything -Werror (with justified exceptions) over the generated cpp output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-cpp-generated-frama-clang-readers" :type :task :title "C++ Frama-Clang on the generated readers (cpp port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-cpp-generated-frama-clang-readers" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-c-cpp" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-cpp" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "70e9bf98222da57b2e0d278f215548e376962271" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-cpp-generated-frama-clang-readers.w1.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-cpp-generated-frama-clang-readers.w1.g1.e21 head 70e9bf98222da57b2e0d278f215548e376962271 (attempt 1, review). Task: C++ Frama-Clang on the generated readers (cpp port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-cpp-generated-frama-clang-readers of stream schema-c-cpp was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: Frama-Clang with Frama-C on the generated C++ readers (the subset Frama-Clang accepts; name what it cannot parse) over the generated cpp output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one). Heavy: nightly only. Fleet already has Frama-Clang work in progress on the fleet-proof-tools stream; reuse its install, do not duplicate it." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-cpp-nightly-fuzz" :type :task :title "nightly fuzzing (cpp port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-cpp-nightly-fuzz" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-c-cpp" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-cpp" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "551bf288015b4997085029073a65bec318a848e8" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-cpp-nightly-fuzz.w7.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-cpp-nightly-fuzz.w7.g1.e21 head 551bf288015b4997085029073a65bec318a848e8 (attempt 7, review). Task: nightly fuzzing (cpp port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-cpp-nightly-fuzz of stream schema-c-cpp was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "NIGHTLY FUZZING (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Fuzz the cpp port's generated readers with its native coverage-guided fuzzer: libFuzzer with ASan, UBSan and MSan. Targets: load, strict read and text/JSON parse for every table in a fuzz corpus schema set (pick the set from the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus) so that every table shape is covered, and list it in a file the harness reads). Seed the fuzzer from the Go fuzz corpus (internal/fuzz/testdata and the go test -fuzz seeds) and the conformance vectors. Run ASan+UBSan and MSan builds in separate nightly runs." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-cpp-resource-bounds" :type :task :title "cpp port: bounded memory and time on hostile inputs (cpp port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-cpp-resource-bounds" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-c-cpp" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-cpp" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-cpp-resource-bounds of stream schema-c-cpp, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "Denial-of-service hardening for the cpp port (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Using the bounds documented by schema-shared-resource-bounds-every-port (read it first), assert in this port that hostile inputs cost bounded memory and time: huge counts, deep nesting, recursion, giant strings and many unknown fields. Allocation is bounded by input size times the documented factor; nesting depth is capped and refused by name. Use a test with an allocation counter in this language (an allocator hook, a counting allocator, runtime memstats, GC counters or the nearest the language offers; name it). Time is asserted by operation count or step count, never by wall clock. A violation is a finding: red first, then fix in the generator or runtime; fix the port, and carry any cross-port gap as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <one line>." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-cpp-runs-hostile-corpus-t" :type :task :title "cpp port runs the whole hostile corpus in its unit tier (cpp port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-cpp-runs-hostile-corpus-t" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-c-cpp" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-cpp" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "e04e6f8405d1e4d9c17599742ec1656a1583e14b" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-cpp-runs-hostile-corpus-t.w3.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-cpp-runs-hostile-corpus-t.w3.g1.e21 head e04e6f8405d1e4d9c17599742ec1656a1583e14b (attempt 3, review). Task: cpp port runs the whole hostile corpus in its unit tier (cpp port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-cpp-runs-hostile-corpus-t of stream schema-c-cpp was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "Make the cpp port run every input of the committed hostile corpus (built by schema-shared-hostile-corpus; read docs/HOSTILE-CORPUS.md and the manifest first) in its unit tier: for each input, the port's generated reader must reach the verdict the manifest holds (accept with the same decoded value digest, or refuse with the same named reason). The runner reads files only (no network, no real time). A mismatch is a finding: red first where it is a reader bug, carried as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <input> <one line>. Do not edit the corpus here; a wrong manifest verdict is reported against the engine card." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-cs-conformance-checked-overflow-t" :type :task :title "C# checked arithmetic over the conformance tests (cs port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-cs-conformance-checked-overflow-t" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-cs" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-cs" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-cs-cook-hash-arithmetic-unchecked,schema-cs-generated-checked-arithmetic" :pushed-head "195eb0b2d3cf561bfc6555dd0e8c51c999d8be78" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-cs-conformance-checked-overflow-t of stream schema-cs, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. It carried an earlier head: schema-cs-conformance-checked-overflow-t attempt 4 head 195eb0b2d3cf561bfc6555dd0e8c51c999d8be78. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: CheckForOverflowUnderflow (checked arithmetic) enabled in the generated C# and the runtime, run through the conformance tests, so overflow bugs become exceptions over the generated cs output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-cs-cook-hash-arithmetic-unchecked" :type :task :title "C#: cs-cook's hash and checksum arithmetic wraps on purpose, under unchecked" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-cs-cook-hash-arithmetic-unchecked" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-cs" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-cs" :tier "heavy" :needs "" :pushed-head "1e654d9f5bee96f33dd9b17c0e72e55b05466511" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-cs-cook-hash-arithmetic-unchecked.w2.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-cs-cook-hash-arithmetic-unchecked.w2.g1.e21 head 1e654d9f5bee96f33dd9b17c0e72e55b05466511 (attempt 2, review). Task: C#: cs-cook's hash and checksum arithmetic wraps on purpose, under unchecked. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-cs-cook-hash-arithmetic-unchecked of stream schema-cs was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE GAP. schema-cs-conformance-checked-overflow-t now builds every assembly checked, and that run hit real System.OverflowException in test/cs-cook/src/Walk.cs:297, Header.Fnv1a64: FNV-1a 64 relies on wrapping multiplication, which a checked build refuses. The raw log is the w3 attempt's conformance log on hetzner2 (01-conformance.log of schema-cs-conformance-checked-overflow-t.w3)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-cs-fixed-tables-are-private-and-immutable" :type :task :title "C# generated fixed tables: private and immutable to callers" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-cs-fixed-tables-are-private-and-immutable" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-cs" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-cs" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "80fb67a15f418faadcad2ac6d903a903bdbcea34" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-cs-fixed-tables-are-private-and-immutable.w3.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-cs-fixed-tables-are-private-and-immutable.w3.g1.e21 head 80fb67a15f418faadcad2ac6d903a903bdbcea34 (attempt 3, review). Task: C# generated fixed tables: private and immutable to callers. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-cs-fixed-tables-are-private-and-immutable of stream schema-cs was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "WHY. The Java SpotBugs lens (card schema-java-generated-spotbugs-gate, triage list triage-findings-medium-unfiltered.xml in its receipts) found 512 real MS_PKGPROTECT findings: generated fixed-table classes expose public static arrays (layout, defaults, dest, known and the like) whose elements any caller can overwrite, corrupting the decode tables for the whole process. Test code in other packages reads these arrays today. Hot read path stays zero-allocation: the generated code reads its own private table directly; only outside callers go through an accessor." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-cs-generated-checked-arithmetic" :type :task :title "C#: generated code is correct under a checked build; every overflow site is triaged" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-cs-generated-checked-arithmetic" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-cs" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-cs" :tier "heavy" :needs "" :pushed-head "b74ad5f3e095e2601c7b92e684c494d4b7ce15a1" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-cs-generated-checked-arithmetic.w2.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-cs-generated-checked-arithmetic.w2.g1.e21 head b74ad5f3e095e2601c7b92e684c494d4b7ce15a1 (attempt 2, review). Task: C#: generated code is correct under a checked build; every overflow site is triaged. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-cs-generated-checked-arithmetic of stream schema-cs was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE GAP. schema-cs-conformance-checked-overflow-t now builds every assembly checked, and the checked conformance run hits OverflowException in generated C#. Examples: testdata/golden/tables/examples-cs/TablesTable.cs:1208 (a scalar conversion) and the Tblrt1Region.cs:2622 UInt128 RetainPut cast. The raw log is the w3 attempt's conformance log on hetzner2 (01-conformance.log of schema-cs-conformance-checked-overflow-t.w3)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
