  (:id "sprint-out/schema-dart-runs-hostile-corpus-t" :type :task :title "dart port runs the whole hostile corpus in its unit tier (dart port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-dart-runs-hostile-corpus-t" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-dart" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-dart" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "9124979a51dbe22a4e9ce49d92d2db864d972bbb" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-dart-runs-hostile-corpus-t.w1.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-dart-runs-hostile-corpus-t.w1.g1.e21 head 9124979a51dbe22a4e9ce49d92d2db864d972bbb (attempt 1, review). Task: dart port runs the whole hostile corpus in its unit tier (dart port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-dart-runs-hostile-corpus-t of stream schema-dart was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "Make the dart port run every input of the committed hostile corpus (built by schema-shared-hostile-corpus; read docs/HOSTILE-CORPUS.md and the manifest first) in its unit tier: for each input, the port's generated reader must reach the verdict the manifest holds (accept with the same decoded value digest, or refuse with the same named reason). The runner reads files only (no network, no real time). A mismatch is a finding: red first where it is a reader bug, carried as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <input> <one line>. Do not edit the corpus here; a wrong manifest verdict is reported against the engine card." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-dart-u64-codec-exact-on-web" :type :task :title "The remaining 64-bit sites in the generated Dart are unsafe under dart2js: union int64 arms, block/home and wide fixed forms lose or corrupt the high bytes between 2^32 and 2^53" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-dart-u64-codec-exact-on-web" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-dart" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-dart" :tier "" :needs "schema-dart-vm-dart2js-differential" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-dart-u64-codec-exact-on-web of stream schema-dart, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "SCOPE (coordinator, 2026-10-19, re-scoped in flight). The putU64/readU64/_signExtend codec fix is kept and verified in schema-dart-vm-dart2js-differential (d861a246); this card does NOT redo it and lands after it. Dart's shifts and bit operators are the 32-bit JavaScript operators on the web, so any shift of 32 or more, or a bit operation on a value that can exceed 2^31, corrupts under dart2js. This card owns the other sites." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-dart-vm-dart2js-differential" :type :task :title "Dart VM versus dart2js differential (dart port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-dart-vm-dart2js-differential" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-dart" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-dart" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "5dd2d7c94e3b6fea81d486b1a32acd1d1ad737ab" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-dart-vm-dart2js-differential.w9.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-dart-vm-dart2js-differential.w9.g1.e21 head 5dd2d7c94e3b6fea81d486b1a32acd1d1ad737ab (attempt 9, review). Task: Dart VM versus dart2js differential (dart port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-dart-vm-dart2js-differential of stream schema-dart was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: a differential between the Dart VM and dart2js/web over the conformance tests: web ints are 53-bit doubles, a real bug lens, so every value above 2^53 must be refused or handled identically over the generated dart output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one). Heavy: nightly only." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate" :type :task :title "Elixir Dialyzer and Credo gate (elixir port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-elixir" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-elixir" :tier "pro" :needs "elixir-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-elixir-generated-dialyzer-credo-gate of stream schema-elixir, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: Dialyzer success typings (cache the PLT) and Credo --strict over the generated Elixir over the generated elixir output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-elixir-nightly-fuzz" :type :task :title "nightly fuzzing (elixir port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-elixir-nightly-fuzz" :sprint-column "ready" :sprint-stream "schema-elixir" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-elixir" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "c9768f2f3acf5b54136345f38cdf183c7c739796" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-elixir-nightly-fuzz.w10.g2.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-elixir-nightly-fuzz.w10.g2.e21 head c9768f2f3acf5b54136345f38cdf183c7c739796 (attempt 11, ready). Task: nightly fuzzing (elixir port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-elixir-nightly-fuzz of stream schema-elixir was in ready, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "NIGHTLY FUZZING (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Fuzz the elixir port's generated readers with its native coverage-guided fuzzer: StreamData-driven mutation of valid encodings. Targets: load, strict read and text/JSON parse for every table in a fuzz corpus schema set (pick the set from the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus) so that every table shape is covered, and list it in a file the harness reads). Seed the fuzzer from the Go fuzz corpus (internal/fuzz/testdata and the go test -fuzz seeds) and the conformance vectors. Generate valid encodings of each table, mutate them (bit flips, truncation, splice, boundary integers), and feed the strict readers." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-elixir-resource-bounds" :type :task :title "elixir port: bounded memory and time on hostile inputs (elixir port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-elixir-resource-bounds" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-elixir" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-elixir" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-elixir-resource-bounds of stream schema-elixir, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "Denial-of-service hardening for the elixir port (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Using the bounds documented by schema-shared-resource-bounds-every-port (read it first), assert in this port that hostile inputs cost bounded memory and time: huge counts, deep nesting, recursion, giant strings and many unknown fields. Allocation is bounded by input size times the documented factor; nesting depth is capped and refused by name. Use a test with an allocation counter in this language (an allocator hook, a counting allocator, runtime memstats, GC counters or the nearest the language offers; name it). Time is asserted by operation count or step count, never by wall clock. A violation is a finding: red first, then fix in the generator or runtime; fix the port, and carry any cross-port gap as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <one line>." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-elixir-streamdata-property-tests" :type :task :title "Elixir StreamData property tests (elixir port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-elixir-streamdata-property-tests" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-elixir" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-elixir" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "8f6af057d675f0b7328ba16de5ede85fcfadd74b" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-elixir-streamdata-property-tests.w3.g3.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-elixir-streamdata-property-tests.w3.g3.e21 head 8f6af057d675f0b7328ba16de5ede85fcfadd74b (attempt 7, review). Task: Elixir StreamData property tests (elixir port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-elixir-streamdata-property-tests of stream schema-elixir was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: StreamData property tests over the generated Elixir: round-trip identity for generated values of every table, and that every strict read of a mutated encoding is a clean refusal over the generated elixir output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-compiler-package-tests-fit-the-budget" :type :task :title "`go test ./compiler/` runs ~540 s unloaded and hits the 600 s timeout on a loaded bench" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-compiler-package-tests-fit-the-budget" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "none" :pushed-head "8277935369b7358099f340836332f82613c618ac" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-go-compiler-package-tests-fit-the-budget.w3.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-go-compiler-package-tests-fit-the-budget.w3.g1.e21 head 8277935369b7358099f340836332f82613c618ac (attempt 3, review). Task: `go test ./compiler/` runs ~540 s unloaded and hits the 600 s timeout on a loaded bench. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-go-compiler-package-tests-fit-the-budget of stream schema-go was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "Source. The coordinator, 2026-10-19: `go test ./compiler/` takes about 540 s on a quiet bench, at head and at base alike, and hits go test's 600 s timeout on a loaded one; with SCHEMA_SLOW=1 it times out reliably. That breaks the one-minute CI rule: a unit test is logic only, with no programs and no real time." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-fuzz-compare-normalised-input-go" :type :task :title "testgen's fuzz comparison, piece 2 (twin): the Go normaliser the wire and text targets compare against" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-fuzz-compare-normalised-input-go" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-go-testgen-fuzz-target-per-table" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-fuzz-compare-normalised-input-go of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "OWNER RULE (Glenn, 2026-10-15 12:34Z): \"When you improve schema, improve the standard, and then fix it in golang and verify the fix. Stop the multi-language stuff until we have finished our dogfooding in golang.\" The rule is written in docs/SPEC-TABLES.md first, in a commit of its own, and Go is then made to match it; no other language's emitter is edited, and every other target refuses a new construct by name, centrally, in compiler/generate.go, as compiler/tablesstringarrays.go does for text lists. Worked example: the landed card schema-string-arrays-and-top-level-array-roots (standard commit, then Go, central refusal, red-then-green tests)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-fuzz-compare-normalised-input-spec" :type :task :title "testgen's fuzz comparison, piece 1: the standard's normalised-input rule and the help sentence" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-fuzz-compare-normalised-input-spec" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-go-testgen-fuzz-target-per-table" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-fuzz-compare-normalised-input-spec of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "OWNER RULE (Glenn, 2026-10-15 12:34Z): \"When you improve schema, improve the standard, and then fix it in golang and verify the fix. Stop the multi-language stuff until we have finished our dogfooding in golang.\" The rule is written in docs/SPEC-TABLES.md first, in a commit of its own, and Go is then made to match it; no other language's emitter is edited, and every other target refuses a new construct by name, centrally, in compiler/generate.go, as compiler/tablesstringarrays.go does for text lists. Worked example: the landed card schema-string-arrays-and-top-level-array-roots (standard commit, then Go, central refusal, red-then-green tests)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-fuzz-enum-variant-ref-unknown-is-legal" :type :task :title "The generated fuzz target treats an enum variant reference to a non-variant id-table entry as a crash; the standard says it is legal (unknown, read as None)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-fuzz-enum-variant-ref-unknown-is-legal" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-go-reader-enum-variant-ref-not-swapped,schema-go-testgen-fuzz-target-per-table" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-fuzz-enum-variant-ref-unknown-is-legal of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "Source. schema-go-reader-enum-variant-ref-not-swapped (attempt 4, read OK, 2026-10-19) found its fuzz crashers are \"case B: harness, not reader\". In both crashers (FuzzLoadoutConfigWire, 212 and 422 bytes, prefix 01011e00030e051e0302020204...) the enum variant reference byte at offset 3 names an id-table entry (entry 3) that is a field-name id (`podium` in the 212-byte sample, `grades` in the 422-byte one), not a variant of the enum. The reader resolves by ENTRY, counts one `unknown` and reads the field as None, exactly as docs/SPEC-TABLES.md section 16.11 and section 4 say it should, and it is not silent. The reader is right. The fuzz target's assertion (decodes to a value whose re-encoding is exactly the input, or refused by name) is wrong for this one legal case: the None read re-encodes with a renumbered id table, so the bytes differ although nothing was misread." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-generated-staticcheck-nilaway-gate" :type :task :title "Go staticcheck and nilaway gate (go port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-generated-staticcheck-nilaway-gate" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "dd83f154e645841b18b6c6f504fc01f993ec1f34" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-go-generated-staticcheck-nilaway-gate.w10.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-go-generated-staticcheck-nilaway-gate.w10.g1.e21 head dd83f154e645841b18b6c6f504fc01f993ec1f34 (attempt 10, review). Task: Go staticcheck and nilaway gate (go port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-go-generated-staticcheck-nilaway-gate of stream schema-go was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: staticcheck and uber nilaway nil-safety analysis over the generated go output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one). Every generated Go unit from the corpus is vetted as its own package; nilaway runs through its multichecker or go vet -vettool." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-int128-from64-sign-extension-tested" :type :task :title "A planted fault that drops the sign extension in gotable's Int128From64 left the whole suite green: no test widens a negative int64 to int128" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-int128-from64-sign-extension-tested" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "c7b97c483b566ee7db461652728ca156dee2d549" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-go-int128-from64-sign-extension-tested.w7.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-go-int128-from64-sign-extension-tested.w7.g1.e21 head c7b97c483b566ee7db461652728ca156dee2d549 (attempt 7, review). Task: A planted fault that drops the sign extension in gotable's Int128From64 left the whole suite green: no test widens a negative int64 to int128. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-go-int128-from64-sign-extension-tested of stream schema-go was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "Source. The coordinator's mutation probe: removing the sign extension from Int128From64 (a negative int64 then widens with Hi = 0 instead of all ones) keeps every test green, SCHEMA_SLOW=1 and the serialize.go sibling present included. No test reaches a negative int64 widened to int128 through the generated Go path or the tabletext path." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-javatable-javac-bounded-and-functional" :type :task :title "javatable tests: javac only in the functional tier, and bounded there" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-javatable-javac-bounded-and-functional" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "f63763f93e93b094ed63f196654255a34ecaf1cb" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-javatable-javac-bounded-and-functional of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. It carried an earlier head: schema-go-javatable-javac-bounded-and-functional attempt 8 head f63763f93e93b094ed63f196654255a34ecaf1cb. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "OWNER RULE (Glenn, restated 2026-10-12): \"Anything that uses real time, network calls, external services, sockets -- that's a functional test.\" Unit tests are lightweight and logic only; a test that runs a program belongs in the functional tier." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-json-base64-canonical" :type :task :title "The JSON form's bytes(N) read refuses non-canonical base64 by name; writers emit canonical base64 only" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-json-base64-canonical" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "de36b2847198f71de0c0701dd7808df17d01f84f" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-go-json-base64-canonical.w10.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-go-json-base64-canonical.w10.g1.e21 head de36b2847198f71de0c0701dd7808df17d01f84f (attempt 13, review). Task: The JSON form's bytes(N) read refuses non-canonical base64 by name; writers emit canonical base64 only. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-go-json-base64-canonical of stream schema-go was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "OWNER RULE (Glenn, 2026-10-15 12:34Z): \"When you improve schema, improve the standard, and then fix it in golang and verify the fix. Stop the multi-language stuff until we have finished our dogfooding in golang.\" The rule is written in docs/SPEC-TABLES.md first, in a commit of its own, and Go is then made to match it; no other language's emitter is edited. This card is the JSON twin of the landed card schema-go-text-base64-canonical, which defines the refusal name and the canonical rule; read that card's section of the standard first and reuse it, never restate a second rule." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-json-integer-fields-read-exactly" :type :task :title "a JSON integer field is read exactly, never through float64, in both Go engines" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-json-integer-fields-read-exactly" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "9c04b30e38a909412c8fae8365ba91e275217fc1" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-json-integer-fields-read-exactly of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. It carried an earlier head: schema-go-json-integer-fields-read-exactly attempt 3 head 9c04b30e38a909412c8fae8365ba91e275217fc1. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "OWNER RULE (Glenn, 2026-10-15): \"When you improve schema, improve the standard, and then fix it in golang and verify the fix. Stop the multi-language stuff until we have finished our dogfooding in golang.\" The standard states the rule first; then Go is fixed and a test proves it. No other language's emitter, runtime or driver is edited.
Source: the comprehensive spec-vs-Go review of 2026-10-18 (Glenn: \"do a *comprehensive* spec review vs. the golang implementation and make sure they match\"). A cold reader found this row at sprint/schema-go d808c3f54, with the Go file and line it read; the coordinator's ruling (under Glenn's delegation, 2026-10-18) follows the reviewer's recommendation: fix Go; the spec rule is right, and Go already reads map keys exactly. Line numbers are as read at d808c3f54 and may have moved a few lines; find the code by the name given." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-json-refuses-lone-surrogates" :type :task :title "Both JSON readers refuse a lone or out-of-order surrogate escape, by name, instead of replacing it silently with U+FFFD" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-json-refuses-lone-surrogates" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-go-jsontestsuite-policy,schema-go-json-hostile-utf8-rows-exempt-unported-legs,cpp-hostile-runner-honours-carried-by" :pushed-head "5b904bdd790fcc56fca091e6e533f554c0324bc3" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-json-refuses-lone-surrogates of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. It carried an earlier head: schema-go-json-refuses-lone-surrogates attempt 11 head 5b904bdd790fcc56fca091e6e533f554c0324bc3. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "This card stands on schema-go-jsontestsuite-policy, which lands first: it vendors JSONTestSuite under testdata/jsontestsuite, writes the policy table as SPEC-TABLES 16.11, rewrites 16.3's read rule to a refusal named `string_lone_surrogate: <key>`, and lists in testdata/jsontestsuite/PENDING.tsv the 10 files this card closes. Read those at your BASE before writing anything; the reason text and the key spelling are 16.11's, not this brief's." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-json-semantic-equal-oracle" :type :task :title "The semantic-equal oracle for JSON texts, by SPEC-TABLES 16.12 (pro)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-json-semantic-equal-oracle" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-go-jsontestsuite-policy,schema-go-json-any-in-variable-table" :pushed-head "4bba827e37a37f25336f4f751f7a7260ffb89ae8" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-go-json-semantic-equal-oracle.w5.g3.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-go-json-semantic-equal-oracle.w5.g3.e21 head 4bba827e37a37f25336f4f751f7a7260ffb89ae8 (attempt 5, review). Task: The semantic-equal oracle for JSON texts, by SPEC-TABLES 16.12 (pro). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-go-json-semantic-equal-oracle of stream schema-go was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "GOAL (Glenn, 2026-10-17): \"If we can match everything there, then we have a very flexible binary variable table format.\" Every JSONTestSuite file the policy accepts (all y_, plus the i_ files 16.11 rules accept) loads into a binary VARIABLE table with no hand-written schema per file, and comes back out equal in value." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-json-unknown-key-strict" :type :task :title "A strict JSON read accepts an unknown key and reports it by key path, as the binary form tolerates an unknown wire id" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-json-unknown-key-strict" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "heavy" :needs "schema-go-strict-read-by-default" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-json-unknown-key-strict of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "OWNER RULE (Glenn, 2026-10-15 12:34Z): \"When you improve schema, improve the standard, and then fix it in golang and verify the fix. Stop the multi-language stuff until we have finished our dogfooding in golang.\" Where this card changes a rule, the rule is written in docs/SPEC-TABLES.md first, in a commit of its own, and Go is then made to match it; no other language's emitter is edited." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-json-utf8-refusal-names-the-key" :type :task :title "the string_not_utf8 refusal names the key that held the bytes, and the harness checks the reason, not just `refused`" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-json-utf8-refusal-names-the-key" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-go-json-hostile-utf8-rows-exempt-unported-legs" :pushed-head "88bf3939dda9244694023078af44e5e57355aefb" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-go-json-utf8-refusal-names-the-key.w2.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-go-json-utf8-refusal-names-the-key.w2.g1.e21 head 88bf3939dda9244694023078af44e5e57355aefb (attempt 2, review). Task: the string_not_utf8 refusal names the key that held the bytes, and the harness checks the reason, not just `refused`. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-go-json-utf8-refusal-names-the-key of stream schema-go was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "OWNER RULE (Glenn, 2026-10-15): \"When you improve schema, improve the standard, and then fix it in golang and verify the fix. Stop the multi-language stuff until we have finished our dogfooding in golang.\" No other language's emitter, runtime or driver is edited." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-json-value-corpus-roundtrip" :type :task :title "In internal/jsontestsuite/roundtrip_test.go, compile a `json = \"value\"` unit with the generator, build and run it with the package's helper in a t.TempDir() (the house pattern for a generated unit), and for every file the policy accepts: JSON to binary (with the integrity trailer) to the strict read to JSON, compared with Equal" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-json-value-corpus-roundtrip" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-go-json-value-tojson,schema-go-json-semantic-equal-oracle" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-json-value-corpus-roundtrip of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE TASK. In internal/jsontestsuite/roundtrip_test.go, compile a `json = \"value\"` unit with the generator, build and run it with the package's helper in a t.TempDir() (the house pattern for a generated unit), and for every file the policy accepts: JSON to binary (with the integrity trailer) to the strict read to JSON, compared with Equal. Reversed witnesses: flip one byte of a binary image and show the strict read refuses it as integrity_mismatch; for each bound row of 16.13, one input past that bound is refused by name at BOTH the JSON step and the binary step (build the binary image by hand where the JSON step already refuses). Files the policy refuses must never reach the binary step: assert that too. Where the harness finds a defect in a lower layer, name it in the report with the file and the layer, and HOLD; do not patch the layers here." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-json-value-declaration" :type :task :title "Read 16.13 and 16.10 at BASE, then in the files PATHS names: (1) accept `json = \"value\"` as the second value of the key's closed vocabulary (it is `\"array\"` alone today), carried on the table in the IR the way `\"array\"` is, and in no projection, build version, lock or tables baseline (as 16.13 says)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-json-value-declaration" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "9d30f506f827939781043b1115ef065935a20c97" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-json-value-declaration of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. It carried an earlier head: schema-go-json-value-declaration attempt 1 head 9d30f506f827939781043b1115ef065935a20c97. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE TASK. Read 16.13 and 16.10 at BASE, then in the files PATHS names: (1) accept `json = \"value\"` as the second value of the key's closed vocabulary (it is `\"array\"` alone today), carried on the table in the IR the way `\"array\"` is, and in no projection, build version, lock or tables baseline (as 16.13 says). (2) Check the declaration by SHAPE and refuse every mismatch by name, `json_value_shape: <Table>: <the first difference>`, exactly as 16.13 lists the shape rules. (3) Refuse a table declared `json = \"value\"` as the target of any pointer (`*T`, `[]*T`, `[..N]*T`, a pointer arm), naming the pointer field. (4) Refuse the construct on every target but Go, centrally in the compiler, by name, in the sentence 16.13 gives: `target \"<target>\" refuses the construct json = \"value\" on table <Table>`, in the place the existing `\"array\"` refusal lives; no other language's emitter is edited. (5) The accepted declaration compiles for Go (no new Go output is required: the codec is the next layers). Where 16.13 and the code disagree on a word, 16.13 rules; if you find 16.13 wrong, stop with HOLD and name the line." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-json-value-fromjson" :type :task :title "In internal/codegen/gotable/json.go, make the Go table emitter's JSON reader, for a table declared `json = \"value\"`, read the raw value (not the wrapped object 16.2 writes) into the tape in ONE pass: nodes in pre-order, key bytes then text bytes in the blob, a number kept as its token bytes (never parsed), a string and key decoded to UTF-8, object member order and duplicate keys kept, depth counted from the file root and refused past 128, a key past 255 decoded bytes refused (never clamped), a number token past 511 bytes refused, string and blob sizes and node count refused at their caps, each by the name 16.13 gives the JSON-step row" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-json-value-fromjson" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-go-json-value-tape-scan" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-json-value-fromjson of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE TASK. In internal/codegen/gotable/json.go, make the Go table emitter's JSON reader, for a table declared `json = \"value\"`, read the raw value (not the wrapped object 16.2 writes) into the tape in ONE pass: nodes in pre-order, key bytes then text bytes in the blob, a number kept as its token bytes (never parsed), a string and key decoded to UTF-8, object member order and duplicate keys kept, depth counted from the file root and refused past 128, a key past 255 decoded bytes refused (never clamped), a number token past 511 bytes refused, string and blob sizes and node count refused at their caps, each by the name 16.13 gives the JSON-step row. Zero nodes is null. The result must pass the L2 scan unchanged. Test: one text per JSON-step row, refused by name; every y_ file in the corpus loads. The writer is the next layer: this card builds no writer. Where 16.13 and the code disagree, 16.13 rules; if it is wrong, stop with HOLD and name the line." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-json-value-tabletext" :type :task :title "In internal/tabletext make the reader and writer handle a table declared `json = \"value\"`: read the raw value to the tape, write the tape back as canonical text, with the bounds and refusal names of 16.13" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-json-value-tabletext" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-go-json-value-tojson" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-json-value-tabletext of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE TASK. In internal/tabletext make the reader and writer handle a table declared `json = \"value\"`: read the raw value to the tape, write the tape back as canonical text, with the bounds and refusal names of 16.13. Test it against the corpus under testdata/jsontestsuite and against the Go-emitted code for the same inputs, including every JSON-step refusal row. Do not change the generated-code emitter (that is L3 and L4, landed); tabletext tests currently red at BASE (name them in the report) stay out of scope. Where 16.13 and the code disagree, 16.13 rules; if it is wrong, stop with HOLD and name the line." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-json-value-tape-scan" :type :task :title "In internal/codegen/gotable/jsonvalue.go write the scan the generated Go loader will call for a tape (a function the emitter can inline or call; the emitter wiring is the next layer's if it needs more than a call): it walks the nodes in pre-order in ONE linear pass, with zero allocations, counting depth from the file root (it is started at the walk's current depth, so a value nested at d=1 hits the cap one level sooner), and refuses by the name 16.13 gives each of the binary-step rows: every length that would run the text blob past its end, a container count past the nodes left, a kind outside the seven, key and number-token caps, string and blob sizes, node count, depth past 128, a Null with a count or length, text bytes left over after the last node" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-json-value-tape-scan" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-go-json-value-declaration" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-json-value-tape-scan of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE TASK. In internal/codegen/gotable/jsonvalue.go write the scan the generated Go loader will call for a tape (a function the emitter can inline or call; the emitter wiring is the next layer's if it needs more than a call): it walks the nodes in pre-order in ONE linear pass, with zero allocations, counting depth from the file root (it is started at the walk's current depth, so a value nested at d=1 hits the cap one level sooner), and refuses by the name 16.13 gives each of the binary-step rows: every length that would run the text blob past its end, a container count past the nodes left, a kind outside the seven, key and number-token caps, string and blob sizes, node count, depth past 128, a Null with a count or length, text bytes left over after the last node. Read the table in 16.13 and take the names and the order of checks from it; do not invent a name. The trailer (integrity, 2.14) is root-only as 16.13 says. Write one test per row with a hand-built wire, plus the depth pins and the allocation pin. Where 16.13 and the code disagree, 16.13 rules; if it is wrong, stop with HOLD and name the line. Do not change json.go, the text step or other targets." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-json-value-tojson" :type :task :title "In internal/codegen/gotable/json.go, make the Go emitter write and measure the raw value for a table declared `json = \"value\"`: the measure equals the write byte for byte, tokens are verbatim, a program-built bad tape (a count past the nodes left, a kind outside the seven, a length past the blob, depth past 128, a token that is not a valid JSON number) returns the refusal (-1 for the measure) and writes nothing" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-json-value-tojson" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-go-json-value-fromjson" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-json-value-tojson of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE TASK. In internal/codegen/gotable/json.go, make the Go emitter write and measure the raw value for a table declared `json = \"value\"`: the measure equals the write byte for byte, tokens are verbatim, a program-built bad tape (a count past the nodes left, a kind outside the seven, a length past the blob, depth past 128, a token that is not a valid JSON number) returns the refusal (-1 for the measure) and writes nothing. Test: measure equals write over every y_ file; write then read gives an equal tape; each bad-tape shape is refused. Where 16.13 and the code disagree, 16.13 rules; if it is wrong, stop with HOLD and name the line." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-message-form-refuses-text-lists" :type :task :title "The message form is emitted for a variable table holding a text list, and the unit's own announcement is then refused (element kind 12)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-message-form-refuses-text-lists" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "none" :pushed-head "cffe5c7db117ac4c1fa05103d3a552b34aa8157f" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-go-message-form-refuses-text-lists.w4.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-go-message-form-refuses-text-lists.w4.g1.e21 head cffe5c7db117ac4c1fa05103d3a552b34aa8157f (attempt 4, review). Task: The message form is emitted for a variable table holding a text list, and the unit's own announcement is then refused (element kind 12). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-go-message-form-refuses-text-lists of stream schema-go was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "RULING (the coordinator, 2026-10-19): SPEC-TABLES §2.13 holds: the message form is INAPPLICABLE to text lists (`[..N]string(M)` and `[..N]?string(M)`, and the unbounded spellings with them). Today Go (and C++) still emit message batches for a variable table containing a text list, and both announcement readers then refuse element kind 12, so the unit's own announcement is refused. Context: cpp-carries-bounded-text-lists attempt w3, head 24bb2379, met it on the C++ side." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-mutation-tool-and-harness" :type :task :title "Mutation testing for the Go table leg: the pinned tool, the targets, the nightly report" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-mutation-tool-and-harness" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "861d9d406ac34675077d8bf46f499d278180931d" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-go-mutation-tool-and-harness.w6.g4.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-go-mutation-tool-and-harness.w6.g4.e21 head 861d9d406ac34675077d8bf46f499d278180931d (attempt 9, review). Task: Mutation testing for the Go table leg: the pinned tool, the targets, the nightly report. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-go-mutation-tool-and-harness of stream schema-go was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE TASK. (1) Choose the tool by trial, not by name: run each candidate on internal/codegen/gotable/messagewrite.go (read) for at most fifteen minutes and record mutants generated, killed, survived, timed out, and minutes; choose the one whose run is reproducible (the same survivors on two runs) and whose test command can be set per target, and say why in tools/mutation/README.md. (2) Pin it in its own module, tools/mutation/go.mod, with a go tool directive (`go get -tool <module>/cmd/<name>@<version>` run inside tools/mutation), so the root go.mod stays free of requirements; run it with `go tool -modfile=tools/mutation/go.mod <name>`. (3) tools/mutation/targets.tsv names each target (file, the test command that kills its mutants, a timeout): the read emitters internal/codegen/gotable/read.go (read) and messageread.go, the write emitters write.go, messagewrite.go and cookwrite.go, and tables/goruntime/goruntime.go (read). Emitter mutants are killed by the generated-unit tests in internal/codegen/gotable (the runGenerated pattern), so each target's command is the package's tests, never a narrower filter that would hide kills; that file is generated (DO NOT EDIT), so its mutants are [...]" :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-mutation-triage-goruntime" :type :task :title "Mutation triage, the shared Go runtime: every survivor a test or a justified equivalent" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-mutation-triage-goruntime" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-go-mutation-tool-and-harness" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-mutation-triage-goruntime of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE TASK. Get the survivor list: when tools/mutation/README.md (read) measures this batch at 90 minutes or less, run `make mutation-go MUTATION_FILES=\"tables/goruntime/goruntime.go\"` on the bench; when it measures more, the coordinator adds the newest mutation-nightly run's SURVIVED lines for these files to this card as a SURVIVORS: line before it is dealt, and with neither, stop at HOLD naming it. Take each survivor in file and line order. For each: apply that one mutant by hand to a scratch copy (or with the tool's single-mutant mode), and either (a) write a test that passes at BASE and fails under the mutant, in the batch's new test file, named for the rule the mutant breaks (never for the mutant), opening with t.Parallel(), and say in the report which survivor it kills; or (b) when the mutant cannot change any observable behaviour, add a row to tools/mutation/equivalent/goruntime.tsv (file, line, mutator, original, why), the why a sentence a reader can check against the code, never \"unreachable\" without the reason. A survivor that is a real defect (the mutant's behaviour is what the standard requires, or neither is) is not triaged here: report it with the standard section, as a [...]" :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
