6-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-nightly-fuzz" :type :task :title "nightly fuzzing (go port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-nightly-fuzz" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "af101731760456a74dba99953b925e579f2da90b" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-go-nightly-fuzz.w9.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-go-nightly-fuzz.w9.g1.e21 head af101731760456a74dba99953b925e579f2da90b (attempt 9, review). Task: nightly fuzzing (go port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-go-nightly-fuzz of stream schema-go was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "NIGHTLY FUZZING (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Fuzz the go port's generated readers with its native coverage-guided fuzzer: native go test -fuzz. Targets: load, strict read and text/JSON parse for every table in a fuzz corpus schema set (pick the set from the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus) so that every table shape is covered, and list it in a file the harness reads). Seed the fuzzer from the Go fuzz corpus (internal/fuzz/testdata and the go test -fuzz seeds) and the conformance vectors. Extend the existing per-table Go fuzz targets (internal/fuzz) so every table in the fuzz corpus set has load, strict-read and text/JSON-parse targets, run nightly with -fuzztime." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-reader-refuses-short-fixed-array-count" :type :task :title "A fixed [N]T array whose wire count is short of N is read silently and re-encoded zero-filled; the strict read refuses it by name" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-reader-refuses-short-fixed-array-count" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-reader-refuses-short-fixed-array-count of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "OWNER RULE (Glenn, 2026-10-15 12:34Z): \"When you improve schema, improve the standard, and then fix it in golang and verify the fix. Stop the multi-language stuff until we have finished our dogfooding in golang.\" The rule is written in docs/SPEC-TABLES.md first, in a commit of its own, and Go is then made to match it; no other language's emitter is edited, and every other target refuses a new construct by name, centrally, in compiler/generate.go, as compiler/tablesstringarrays.go does for text lists. Worked example: the landed card schema-string-arrays-and-top-level-array-roots (standard commit, then Go, central refusal, red-then-green tests)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-resource-bounds" :type :task :title "go port: bounded memory and time on hostile inputs (go port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-resource-bounds" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-resource-bounds of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "Denial-of-service hardening for the go port (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Using the bounds documented by schema-shared-resource-bounds-every-port (read it first), assert in this port that hostile inputs cost bounded memory and time: huge counts, deep nesting, recursion, giant strings and many unknown fields. Allocation is bounded by input size times the documented factor; nesting depth is capped and refused by name. Use a test with an allocation counter in this language (an allocator hook, a counting allocator, runtime memstats, GC counters or the nearest the language offers; name it). Time is asserted by operation count or step count, never by wall clock. A violation is a finding: red first, then fix in the generator or runtime; fix the port, and carry any cross-port gap as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <one line>." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-runs-hostile-corpus-t" :type :task :title "go port runs the whole hostile corpus in its unit tier (go port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-runs-hostile-corpus-t" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "62534b739665c51bf2d7df458f8cb45c5b696159" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-go-runs-hostile-corpus-t.w4.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-go-runs-hostile-corpus-t.w4.g1.e21 head 62534b739665c51bf2d7df458f8cb45c5b696159 (attempt 5, review). Task: go port runs the whole hostile corpus in its unit tier (go port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-go-runs-hostile-corpus-t of stream schema-go was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "Make the go port run every input of the committed hostile corpus (built by schema-shared-hostile-corpus; read docs/HOSTILE-CORPUS.md and the manifest first) in its unit tier: for each input, the port's generated reader must reach the verdict the manifest holds (accept with the same decoded value digest, or refuse with the same named reason). The runner reads files only (no network, no real time). A mismatch is a finding: red first where it is a reader bug, carried as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <input> <one line>. Do not edit the corpus here; a wrong manifest verdict is reported against the engine card." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-spec-limits-two-way-bounds" :type :task :title "Go: every spec limit gets an accept test and a refuse test, tied to the enforced constant (go port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-spec-limits-two-way-bounds" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "408f284dae21c45204c6f415819e83ebe0cb4f6d" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-go-spec-limits-two-way-bounds.w7.g2.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-go-spec-limits-two-way-bounds.w7.g2.e21 head 408f284dae21c45204c6f415819e83ebe0cb4f6d (attempt 7, review). Task: Go: every spec limit gets an accept test and a refuse test, tied to the enforced constant (go port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-go-spec-limits-two-way-bounds of stream schema-go was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "Glenn, 2026-10-18: schema must be bulletproof. A read of the spec limits against the Go code found these gaps; close all of them. (1) blob_cap (2^32-1) is not tied to the check that enforces it at internal/codegen/gotable/unboundedtext.go:122, so a planted `>0xfffffffe` passed the tests: derive the check from the one constant and test both sides. (2) The Go arena size is checked only under SCHEMA_SLOW: make the check run in the normal tier (a pure function over sizes, no allocation of the real arena in a unit test). (3) Add two-way runtime tests (at the limit accepts, one past refuses by its NAME) for: blob_cap; json_max_depth 128 accepts and 129 refuses; message_skip_depth (today only a source-string test pins it); a wrong cook_magic refused in Go; int32_extent_cap at the cap; storage_cap one past; fixed_record_bound accept side; fixed_remap_max accept side; and the text defaults 65536, 8192, 4096 and 65536 at the exact bound (read the spec for which limit each default is). (4) The gate command runs ./test/go-tables from the repo root, which is wrong because it is a separate module (test/go-tables/go.mod): fix it to cd test/go-tables first (see make/go.mk, which already does so fo [...]" :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-spec-refusal-names-cross-check" :type :task :title "A test fails when Go has a refusal name the spec lacks, or the spec has one Go lacks" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-spec-refusal-names-cross-check" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "spec-go-s6-5-one-refusal-enum,schema-go-fold-fixed-reasons-into-refuse-enum,schema-go-prose-reasons-become-names" :pushed-head "4b70a1c82cbf438cfe2d2a7b7590ba5f6353fad9" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-go-spec-refusal-names-cross-check.w1.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-go-spec-refusal-names-cross-check.w1.g1.e21 head 4b70a1c82cbf438cfe2d2a7b7590ba5f6353fad9 (attempt 1, review). Task: A test fails when Go has a refusal name the spec lacks, or the spec has one Go lacks. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-go-spec-refusal-names-cross-check of stream schema-go was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "OWNER RULE (Glenn, 2026-10-15): \"When you improve schema, improve the standard, and then fix it in golang and verify the fix.\" No other language's emitter is edited.
Source: the comprehensive spec-vs-Go review of 2026-10-18 (Glenn: \"do a *comprehensive* spec review vs. the golang implementation and make sure they match\"; and \"if any change made in golang has not been folded back into the spec, do that NOW\": the language ports are unheld and read the spec). Every row below was found by a cold reader at sprint/schema-go d808c3f54, with the Go file and line it read." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-testgen-fuzz-target-per-table" :type :task :title "testgen emits a fuzz target per table: no panic, and every flip refused by name or canonical" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-testgen-fuzz-target-per-table" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-go-testgen-round-trip-and-damage,schema-go-wire-bool-not-0-or-1,schema-go-text-base64-canonical,schema-go-json-refuses-invalid-utf8,schema-go-reader-refuses-short-fixed-array-count,schema-go-reader-enum-variant-ref-not-swapped" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-testgen-fuzz-target-per-table of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "BOUNDED SEED CORPUS (Rowan, 2026-10-18; the harness stays, this bounds only what it seeds). Pass 5 found the unbounded corpus unbuildable: one WideBlob sample of about 280k bytes, with a 0, 1 and 0xff mutation at every byte, reached 94 GiB RSS and millions of f.Add cases. So, per table (per Fuzz<Table>Wire, Text and Json target):
- Emit at most 256 mutation seeds, chosen deterministically: the first 16 and last 16 byte positions, then a fixed stride over the positions between them, each position taking all three values 0, 1 and 0xff, stopping at the cap. Where the stride set is smaller than the cap, all of it is emitted. The unmutated sample encoding is always also seeded.
- No sample used for seeding exceeds 4 KiB. A larger sample is trimmed to a representative 4 KiB (the first 2 KiB and the last 2 KiB) before it is seeded or mutated, and the generated code carries a comment saying so. Trimming is for seeding only; the round-trip tests keep the full sample.
- A test pins the seed count (at most 256 per target) and the total seed bytes across the generated file, so the corpus cannot silently grow again; the test fails when either exceeds its pinned bound.
- Peak RSS of `go test` of [...]" :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-unlocked-builder-write-refuses" :type :task :title "Writing a builder's unlocked root with no arena refuses by name instead of writing zeros" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-unlocked-builder-write-refuses" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "1b19f59d351323ae61904b334c7146547a9ddf23" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-unlocked-builder-write-refuses of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. It carried an earlier head: schema-go-unlocked-builder-write-refuses attempt 4 head 1b19f59d351323ae61904b334c7146547a9ddf23. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "OWNER RULE (Glenn, 2026-10-15 12:34Z): \"When you improve schema, improve the standard, and then fix it in golang and verify the fix. Stop the multi-language stuff until we have finished our dogfooding in golang.\" Where this card changes a rule, the rule is written in docs/SPEC-TABLES.md first, in a commit of its own, and Go is then made to match it; no other language's emitter is edited." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-go-writer-refusal-names-the-field" :type :task :title "A writer's refusal names its reason but not the Table.field it refused at" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-go-writer-refusal-names-the-field" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-go" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-go" :tier "pro" :needs "none" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-go-writer-refusal-names-the-field of stream schema-go, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "Source. The coordinator, 2026-10-19. The C++ deprecated-enum card has deferred its field naming to this card." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-java-emitter-nullness-annotations" :type :task :title "The Java emitter writes the null-sentinel pattern without nullness annotations: NullAway reports 19,789 findings on the generated corpus" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-java-emitter-nullness-annotations" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-java" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java" :tier "heavy" :needs "" :pushed-head "07567e3b5f1ea9c1b7b891d1f89ff2dafb09886d" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-java-emitter-nullness-annotations.w2.g2.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-java-emitter-nullness-annotations.w2.g2.e21 head 07567e3b5f1ea9c1b7b891d1f89ff2dafb09886d (attempt 4, review). Task: The Java emitter writes the null-sentinel pattern without nullness annotations: NullAway reports 19,789 findings on the generated corpus. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-java-emitter-nullness-annotations of stream schema-java was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "RULING (coordinator, 2026-10-19, on j29257): the NullAway corpus gate (schema-java-generated-errorprone-nullaway-gate) is red on 19,789 findings, all from the null-sentinel pattern in generated Java. We do NOT blanket-suppress them. The javatable emitter emits nullness annotations instead. The gate card waits on this one: it cannot pass without the annotations." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-java-fixed-tables-are-private-and-immutable" :type :task :title "Java generated fixed tables: private and immutable to callers" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-java-fixed-tables-are-private-and-immutable" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-java" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "f7328d5b38aa74cb0d9172b6d28bd89ab91dc036" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-java-fixed-tables-are-private-and-immutable.w4.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-java-fixed-tables-are-private-and-immutable.w4.g1.e21 head f7328d5b38aa74cb0d9172b6d28bd89ab91dc036 (attempt 4, review). Task: Java generated fixed tables: private and immutable to callers. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-java-fixed-tables-are-private-and-immutable of stream schema-java was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "WHY. The Java SpotBugs lens (card schema-java-generated-spotbugs-gate, triage list triage-findings-medium-unfiltered.xml in its receipts) found 512 real MS_PKGPROTECT findings: generated fixed-table classes expose public static arrays (layout, defaults, dest, known and the like) whose elements any caller can overwrite, corrupting the decode tables for the whole process. Test code in other packages reads these arrays today. Hot read path stays zero-allocation: the generated code reads its own private table directly; only outside callers go through an accessor." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-java-generated-checker-signedness" :type :task :title "Java Checker Framework signedness checker (java port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-java-generated-checker-signedness" :sprint-column "ready" :sprint-stream "schema-java" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "497cf90c8c46310e5685d611fe17b88f5a24570e" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-java-generated-checker-signedness.w3.g3.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-java-generated-checker-signedness.w3.g3.e21 head 497cf90c8c46310e5685d611fe17b88f5a24570e (attempt 9, ready). Task: Java Checker Framework signedness checker (java port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-java-generated-checker-signedness of stream schema-java was in ready, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: the Checker Framework signedness checker over the generated Java: unsigned bytes, shorts and ints held in signed Java types are a prime bug class, so annotate the generator output with @Unsigned/@Signed and let the checker prove every widening, comparison and shift over the generated java output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one). Add PMD in the same target if it takes under an hour; otherwise say so and leave it for a later card." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-java-generated-errorprone-nullaway-gate" :type :task :title "Java Error Prone and NullAway gate (java port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-java-generated-errorprone-nullaway-gate" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-java" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java" :tier "" :needs "schema-java-emitter-nullness-annotations" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-java-generated-errorprone-nullaway-gate of stream schema-java, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: Error Prone and NullAway as javac plugins over the generated Java (warnings as errors, justified suppressions only) over the generated java output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-java-generated-spotbugs-gate" :type :task :title "Java SpotBugs gate (java port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-java-generated-spotbugs-gate" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-java" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "8e9c6f31a4c5c449fbdb851543d3ca19db938d7a" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-java-generated-spotbugs-gate of stream schema-java, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. It carried an earlier head: schema-java-generated-spotbugs-gate attempt 1 head 8e9c6f31a4c5c449fbdb851543d3ca19db938d7a. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "THE LENS. Schema generates the same algorithm in many languages, so every language's strictest checker, run over the generated output for the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus), is a separate lens on bugs (Glenn, 2026-10-18; ideas roadmap group schema-per-language-lenses). THIS CARD: SpotBugs (with the find-sec-bugs plugin) over the compiled generated Java, at the strictest effort/threshold that is not noise-dominated over the generated java output (readers and writers, and the runtime where the port has one)." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-java-nightly-fuzz" :type :task :title "nightly fuzzing (java port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-java-nightly-fuzz" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-java" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "71687d278a2f8d11815fef63aaf43503ce15e2d2" :pushed-branch "sprint/schema-java-nightly-fuzz.w1.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/schema-java-nightly-fuzz.w1.g1.e21 head 71687d278a2f8d11815fef63aaf43503ce15e2d2 (attempt 1, review). Task: nightly fuzzing (java port of schema). Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card schema-java-nightly-fuzz of stream schema-java was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "NIGHTLY FUZZING (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Fuzz the java port's generated readers with its native coverage-guided fuzzer: Jazzer. Targets: load, strict read and text/JSON parse for every table in a fuzz corpus schema set (pick the set from the schema repository's test-schema corpus (every schema under the corpus directories the Makefile's generate targets read, found with grep -n in the Makefile and make/*.mk; do not invent a second corpus) so that every table shape is covered, and list it in a file the harness reads). Seed the fuzzer from the Go fuzz corpus (internal/fuzz/testdata and the go test -fuzz seeds) and the conformance vectors. Use Jazzer fuzz targets (fuzzerTestOneInput) per reader kind." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-java-resource-bounds" :type :task :title "java port: bounded memory and time on hostile inputs (java port of schema)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-java-resource-bounds" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-java" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java" :tier "pro" :needs "" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-java-resource-bounds of stream schema-java, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "Denial-of-service hardening for the java port (Glenn, 2026-10-18). Using the bounds documented by schema-shared-resource-bounds-every-port (read it first), assert in this port that hostile inputs cost bounded memory and time: huge counts, deep nesting, recursion, giant strings and many unknown fields. Allocation is bounded by input size times the documented factor; nesting depth is capped and refused by name. Use a test with an allocation counter in this language (an allocator hook, a counting allocator, runtime memstats, GC counters or the nearest the language offers; name it). Time is asserted by operation count or step count, never by wall clock. A violation is a finding: red first, then fix in the generator or runtime; fix the port, and carry any cross-port gap as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <one line>." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-java-runs-hostile-corpus" :type :task :title "java port runs the whole hostile corpus in its unit tier (java port of schema)" :state :done :evidence ("java/hostile-corpus: make schema-java-runs-hostile-corpus") :sprint-card "schema-java-runs-hostile-corpus" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-java" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-java" :tier "pro" :needs "schema-shared-hostile-corpus,java-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-java-runs-hostile-corpus of stream schema-java, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "Make the java port run every input of the committed hostile corpus (built by schema-shared-hostile-corpus; read docs/HOSTILE-CORPUS.md and the manifest first) in its unit tier: for each input, the port's generated reader must reach the verdict the manifest holds (accept with the same decoded value digest, or refuse with the same named reason). The runner reads files only (no network, no real time). A mismatch is a finding: red first where it is a reader bug, carried as FIX-CARD: <slug>: <input> <one line>. Do not edit the corpus here; a wrong manifest verdict is reported against the engine card." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  (:id "sprint-out/schema-js-checkjs-codec-literals-match-descriptor-type" :type :task :title "checkJs strict: codec and union literals do not match the shared descriptor type (~1,760 findings)" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "schema-js-checkjs-codec-literals-match-descriptor-type" :sprint-column "waiting" :sprint-stream "schema-js" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-js" :tier "heavy" :needs "schema-js-emitter-jsdoc-types" :pushed-head "" :pushed-branch "" :note "Waiting card schema-js-checkjs-codec-literals-match-descriptor-type of stream schema-js, deferred out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: not for the rocketnet v1.0.0 release; moved to the roadmap) with nova-sprint defer; not started in the sprint. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief as defer wrote it." :task "Source. The coordinator, 2026-10-19. Card schema-js-emitter-jsdoc-types (branch sprint/schema-js-emitter-jsdoc-types.w1.g1.e21, head 2b130c5e3) brought `tsc --checkJs --strict` over the generated JS corpus from 41,066 findings to 7,642 with JSDoc only; its report (NOT DONE 1) names the groups that remain, all needing real code changes. Card name of the whole: schema-js-checkjs-strict-to-zero, split into one card per group plus a last card that sets the gate's ratchet to 0. This card is one group. Real code changes in the JS emitter and the runtimes it emits are allowed. THE HARD RULE: the wire bytes stay byte-identical." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
