  (:id "sprint-out/shared-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :type :task :title "sprint/schema-shared takes sprint/schema-go: the shared (C, C#, Go) base forward-merge" :state :todo :evidence nil :sprint-card "shared-base-forward-merge-schema-go" :sprint-column "review" :sprint-stream "schema-shared" :sprint-base "sprint/schema-shared" :tier "heavy" :needs "none" :pushed-head "6ee38419f94ca162744fc2da407debf35a6c6370" :pushed-branch "sprint/shared-base-forward-merge-schema-go.w4.g1.e21" :note "Carried: branch sprint/shared-base-forward-merge-schema-go.w4.g1.e21 head 6ee38419f94ca162744fc2da407debf35a6c6370 (attempt 6, review). Task: sprint/schema-shared takes sprint/schema-go: the shared (C, C#, Go) base forward-merge. Moved out of the sprint on 2026-10-19 (Glenn: \"Please take all work in the current sprint that is not for this rocketnet release and push it out to the appropriate roadmap sexp\"): sprint card shared-base-forward-merge-schema-go of stream schema-shared was in review, not landed; the card was dropped from the sprint naming this item, and its pushed head stays on that branch. :brief-file holds the card's whole brief at the move." :task "ROUTE NOTE (coordinator, 2026-10-19; why attempts 3 and 4 held). The same finding twice (r3, w4): the head merged a sprint/schema-go tip that was already stale by finish time, so make generated-current failed on generated/bench/{paired,tables}/go (BenchTable.go, BenchTableTable.go and the Cook files). schema-go lands faster than one attempt, so STEP 4b now re-merges the current tip just before finishing and DONE-WHEN judges generated-current against the sha the report names. The carried head 972c47687 (merges of schema-go f8610854 at 13b43736 and ba0e3802 at 972c4768, plus a211d995 skip-absent-optional-cook-storage) is sound in source: BASE sprint/schema-shared 1b2da66e is its ancestor and merge-tree is clean; it is 13 commits behind the schema-go tip ac4dc34b as of this note, so STEP 4b applies at once. Keep base fix #526 (7207fa18: c, cs and cpp carry optional-over-variable; r1 caught a resolution dropping it). PATHS: the standing forward-merge ruling grants merge-carried files byte-identical to the merged parent; PATHS lists the real 1238 changed files as subdirectory globs (never a bare internal/**), and NEW names the files of the directories new at BASE." :brief-file "docs/roadmap-briefs/schema-cards-out-2026-10-19.sexp")
  ; Pit stop 2026-10-20 (Glenn: "Archive everything from the sprint that isn't rocketnet. Move the cards into their respective roadmaps."): every unlanded card of the schema streams was dropped from the sprint, its card, findings and brief kept in ~/rowan-working/sprint-archive-2026-10-20/<stream>/<id>.md. Cards building a feature of cpp/c/cs/go/rust/java/js/dart/elixir hold that language's cell ❌ with a note naming them. Goose, Lobster, Lua and Squirrel have no column yet (TestEveryTableHasNineLanguages; each port's roadmap-column card adds it), so their feature cards are tasks below naming the cell they fill (:roadmap-cell), beside the cards that build no feature row (a base fix, CI, a bench, a forward-merge; :roadmap-cell none).
