  ; FINITE TABLE FLOATS (Glenn, 2026-10-27: "Tables go finite-only too, same rule as packets. NaN/inf refused on write and read, -0 and subnormals kept; overturn the 10-18/19 table NaN rule."). One card per leg; docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §3.3 is the rule and the three rulings of 2026-10-27 (compressed floats, no-walk block and cook reads, retained float entries) are in it.
  (:id "tables-finite/shared" :type :task :title "Finite table floats: the enum spelling non_finite_float, the oracle engines refuse a NaN or an infinity on write and on read, and the shared gates hold the rule" :state :done :evidence ("internal/tablewire/floatnan_test.go TestOracleRefusesEachNonFinitePattern" "internal/tablewire/floatnan_test.go TestOracleRetainedFloatIsTested" "internal/tablecook/floatnan_test.go TestACookRefusesANonFiniteFloat" "internal/ci/schema_shared_hostile_corpus_test.go TestSchemaSharedHostileCorpus" "test/conformance/harness/wirefuzz_test.go TestWireVerdictNonFiniteIsARefusal") :roadmap-cell "none" :note "Card 0 of the finite-tables plan. The reference's NaN pins (testdata/wire/tables/floats_nan.bin, the fixedform corpus fu1/fu2 heat and old_float_widen) stay as the C++ writer emits them until tables-finite/cpp; the Go leg reads them as must-refuse vectors.")
  (:id "tables-finite/go" :type :task :title "Go tables are finite only: every read refuses a NaN or an infinity on its raw bits as non_finite_float, every writer refuses one, -0 and subnormals ride" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/gotable/floatspecial_test.go TestGoPlainFloatSpecialValuesAgreeAcrossForms" "internal/codegen/gotable/cfloat_special_values_test.go TestCompressedFloatSpecialValuesEveryForm" "internal/codegen/gotable/fixedcfloat_test.go TestFixedCFloatNonFiniteIsRefused" "internal/codegen/gotable/wire_test.go TestWireSignalingNaNWideningAndLEBOverflow" "test/conformance/go/rows/Float32ValuesValidData_test.go TestRowFloat32ValuesNonFiniteRefused") :roadmap-cell "none" :note "Card 1. Go's block rows and cooked records are the caller's structs read in place, so ruling 2's accessor latch has no site on this leg; the cook's strict validator is schema cook-check, which refuses.")
  (:id "tables-finite/cpp" :type :task :title "C++ tables are finite only: every read refuses a NaN or an infinity on its raw bits as non_finite_float, every writer refuses one, -0 rides by its bits" :state :done :evidence ("test/tables/floatnan_main.cpp make tables-float-nan" "Makefile tables-float-nan-negative-control" "test/conformance/cpp/rows/R21.cpp" "test/tables/versioning_numbers.cpp float_widen_case" "test/tables/fixedform_main.cpp fu_refusal_case" "internal/codegen/cpptable/fixedroadmap_t03_test.go t03R21" "compiler/tablewidencpp_test.go TestCppTableFloatRungIsTheFiniteTestAndTheConversion") :roadmap-cell "none" :note "Card 2. testdata/wire/tables/floats_nan.bin is frozen as the shared must-refuse vector; fixedform_dump.cpp's fu1/fu2 heat (a subnormal, a -0, 1.5) and old_float_widen (-1234.5625) are finite, and the hand-made refusal record is forged from old_float_widen.bin by the leg's own test rather than shipped in the shared corpus. The wire fuzzer's --finite-owed tables-finite/cpp is gone. C++ block rows and cooked records are the caller's structs read in place (no decoding accessor), so ruling 2's latch has no site on this leg; the cook writer refuses. The C++ report names the refusal, not the field.")
  (:id "tables-finite/c" :type :task :title "C tables are finite only: every read refuses a NaN or an infinity on its raw bits as non_finite_float, every writer refuses one, -0 rides by its bits" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/ctable/finitefloat_test.go TestCFiniteFloats" "internal/codegen/ctable/finitefloat_test.go TestCFiniteFloatNegativeControl" "compiler/tablescwire_test.go TestCTableWireWidening" "compiler/tablecensusc_test.go TestCTableFloatRungIsTheFiniteTestAndTheConversion") :roadmap-cell "none" :note "Card 3. The value, region, builder and retaining reads, the message batches (count 0) and the fixed form (a finite pass over storage before the bounds pass, both plans) refuse a NaN or an infinity from its raw bits: refused, reason SCHEMA_TABLE_NON_FINITE_FLOAT, TableReport.non_finite_floats counted, nothing lands, and the strict reads answer SCHEMA_TABLE_REFUSE_NON_FINITE_FLOAT (ordinal 23), set at last. A retained unknown kind 10/11 entry is tested like a known one (ruling 3); a compressed float is tested before its bounds and refused before it is quantized (ruling 1). Every writer refuses one: the file and graph measure/save, the message measure/save, the fixed save (a pre-pass) and the cook. Elision of a plain float compares bits, so -0 rides under a +0 default. table_wire_widen_f32 and its census are gone. TestCTableWireWidening carries the NaN rung again as a must-refuse case. --finite-owed tables-finite/c is dropped from make/c.mk; the control is tables-c-finite-float-negative-control. C block rows and cooked records are the caller's structs read in place with no decoding accessor, so ruling 2's latch has no site on this leg. The C report names the refusal, not the field: it carries no field names for any refusal.")
