  (:id "tables-finite/cs" :type :task :title "C# tables are finite only: every read refuses a NaN or an infinity on its raw bits as non_finite_float, every writer refuses one, -0 rides by its bits" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/cstable/finite_test.go TestCsFiniteFloatRule" "internal/codegen/cstable/fixedroadmap_t04_test.go TestFixedRoadmapCSharpT04Versions" "internal/codegen/cstable/fixedversioning_test.go TestFixedVersioning" "internal/codegen/cstable/fixedversioning_test.go TestCsManifestNonFinite") :roadmap-cell "none" :note "Card 5. The C# leg's own checks are test/cs-tables/src/FiniteChecks.cs (form 1, region, message, region message, fixed, cook) and test/conformance/cs/rows/R21; the control is tables-cs-finite-float-negative-control; --finite-owed tables-finite/cs is gone from make/cs.mk, so the four wire-fuzz bindings compare the refusal. C#'s block rows and cooked records are the caller's structs read in place, so ruling 2's accessor latch has no site on this leg. The float_widen versioning row reads the reference's old_float_widen.bin as must-refuse while its manifest spells a NaN, owed back to an identity row by tables-finite/cpp.")
  (:id "tables-finite/java" :type :task :title "Java tables are finite only: every read refuses a NaN or an infinity on its raw bits as non_finite_float, every writer refuses one, -0 rides by its bits" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/javatable/finitefloat_test.go TestJavaFiniteFloats" "internal/codegen/javatable/finitefloat_test.go TestJavaFiniteFloatNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/javatable/fixedroadmap_t03_test.go TestFixedRoadmapT03Versions" "internal/codegen/javatable/fixedversioning_test.go TestFixedVersioningRows") :roadmap-cell "none" :note "Card 6. Variable, retaining, message and fixed reads refuse from the raw bits (a retained unknown kind 10/11 entry too, ruling 3); every writer refuses; elision compares raw bits. Java's block and cook accessors are static over (data, at) with no view object, so ruling 2's refusal is the thrown TableBytes.NonFiniteFloat naming the field; Java carries no block/cook strict validator. --finite-owed tables-finite/java is dropped from make/java.mk. The corpus rows that still read the C++ reference's NaN (fu1/fu2 heat, old_float_widen) are must-refuse by the manifest until tables-finite/cpp.")
