  (:id "tables-finite/dart" :type :task :title "Dart tables are finite only: every read refuses a NaN or an infinity on its raw bits as non_finite_float, every writer refuses one, -0 rides by its bits" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/darttable/finitefloat_test.go TestDartFiniteFloatsEveryForm" "internal/codegen/darttable/finitefloat_test.go TestDartFiniteFloatNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/darttable/float32_cells_test.go TestDartFloat32CellsAreBitTransparent" "internal/codegen/darttable/fixedcorpus_roundtrip_test.go TestFixedFloat32ArrayWordViewsPreserveBits" "internal/codegen/darttable/fixedroadmap_t04_test.go TestFixedRoadmapDartT04Versions") :roadmap-cell "none" :note "A card of the finite-tables plan, after tables-finite/go. --finite-owed tables-finite/dart is dropped from make/dart.mk. Ruling 2: the block and cook float accessors never return a NaN or an infinity; they answer 0 and latch non_finite_float on the view (nonFiniteFloat), the field named; the Dart leg has no cook or block strict validator of its own. The corpus rows that read the reference's NaN pins (fu1/fu2 heat, old_float_widen) are must-refuse by the manifest until tables-finite/cpp turns the corpus finite.")
